IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg2-support`
IMPORT `dg2-powers`
IMPORT `dg2-registered-agent`
IMPORT `dg2-registered-agent-changes`
IMPORT `dg2-board`
IMPORT `dg2-board-committees`
IMPORT `dg2-board-action`
IMPORT `dg2-officers`
IMPORT `dg2-interested-definitions`
IMPORT `dg2-interested-transactions`
IMPORT `dg2-indemnification`
IMPORT `dg2-board-approvals`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, sections 121 to 147 (Subchapters II, III and IV) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation under the General Corporation Law: an incorporator, a
-- director or officer, a stockholder including a minority stockholder. They ask what the Law lets them do, what it requires of them, what
-- they may require of the corporation, and what can be done to them.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person would ask. Nothing here
-- is new law and no rule is restated: every question calls a layer-1 rule. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates, and
-- the modules' own choices), one for each fact the person states, each with an @desc worded as they would be asked; the records the
-- layer-1 rules take are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers. Where a rule has no answer, because the text
-- does not say, the question answers NOTHING (a MAYBE BOOLEAN), and the @desc of the question says so.
--
-- OFFICIALS: the Secretary of State, the Court of Chancery, the Attorney General and the Department of Education have no seat. Their powers
-- appear as what the person is owed, or exposed to (for example "Can the Secretary refuse to file a document my registered agent
-- submitted?"). Judgments the Law hands to someone else ("in the judgment of the directors", "the court deems it equitable", "the board has
-- determined") are asked as facts about what that body decided.
--
-- THE OTHER PARTY OF EACH RELATION. A right of the person is a duty of the other party, and the facts about the other party that the text
-- makes decisive are inputs (whether the corporation received an undertaking, whether the committee was designated by the board, whether the
-- registered agent kept the information...). Where the Law also puts a duty or a liability on the person, the paired question is asked:
-- "Must my corporation indemnify this person?" and "Am I entitled to be indemnified?" are one rule asked from the two ends.
--
-- Where the Law leaves a figure to the certificate or the bylaws (a quorum, a greater vote) the question asks where it was fixed and what
-- number it fixed. Where it counts directors, it counts votes if the certificate gives a director more or less than one vote (s 141(d)).

§ `Delaware General Corporation Law, ss 121 to 147 -- the questions of a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock`

§§ `Powers (ss 121 to 127)`

-- s 121(a). A corporation, its officers, directors and stockholders possess every power or privilege that this chapter, any other law or the
-- certificate grants, and the powers incidental to them, so far as they are necessary or convenient to the business or purposes in the certificate.
@export Do my corporation, its officers, directors and stockholders possess and may they exercise this power (s 121(a))?
GIVEN `the Law grants it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the power or privilege granted by the General Corporation Law?
      `another law grants it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it granted by any other law?
      `our certificate grants it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it granted by our certificate of incorporation?
      `it is incidental` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it incidental to a power or privilege granted in one of those ways?
      `it serves our purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of the business or purposes set out in our certificate of incorporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my corporation, its officers, directors and stockholders possess and may they exercise this power` IF
    `s 121(a) the corporation, its officers, directors and stockholders possess and may exercise the power or privilege` `the Law grants it` `another law grants it` `our certificate grants it` `it is incidental` `it serves our purposes`

-- s 121(b). Every corporation is governed by the chapter and subject to its restrictions and liabilities.
-- The Law does not say for a corporation organized under another law (answer: nothing).
@export Is my corporation governed by the General Corporation Law and subject to its restrictions and liabilities (s 121(b))?
GIVEN `my corporation is organized under the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation organized under the Delaware General Corporation Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation governed by the General Corporation Law and subject to its restrictions and liabilities` IS
    `s 121(b) the corporation is governed by the provisions and subject to the restrictions and liabilities of this chapter` `my corporation is organized under the Law`

-- s 122. The eighteen specific powers.
-- Answer nothing for a corporation not created under the Law, and for a participation that is neither an association nor a transaction.
@export Does my corporation have this specific power (s 122)?
GIVEN `the power` IS A `s 122 Specific power` @desc Which power? One of the eighteen in s 122, named by paragraph: perpetual succession (1); suing (2); a seal (3); property (4); officers (5); bylaws (6); dissolving (7); doing business elsewhere (8); donations (9); being an incorporator (10); participating with others (11); business in aid of governmental authority (12); contracts and borrowing (13); lending and investing (14); pensions and plans (15); life insurance (16); renouncing opportunities (17); contracts with stockholders (18)
      `my corporation was created under the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your corporation created under the Delaware General Corporation Law?
      `our certificate states a limited duration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation state a limited period of duration?
      `the participation is in an association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you ask about participating with others (11): is it in a corporation, partnership, limited partnership, joint venture or other association of any kind?
      `the participation is in a transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you ask about participating with others (11): is it in a transaction, undertaking or arrangement?
      `we could do it by ourselves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a transaction, undertaking or arrangement: would your corporation have power to conduct it by itself?
      `the business is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you ask about business in aid of governmental authority (12): is the business lawful?
      `the board found it in aid of government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your board of directors found the business to be in aid of governmental authority?
      `the lending is for our corporate purposes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you ask about lending money (14): is the lending for your corporation's corporate purposes?
      `the insurance is for our benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you ask about life insurance (16): is the insurance for your corporation's benefit?
      `whose life is insured` IS A `s 122(16) Whose life is insured` @desc Whose life is insured? One of: the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation; the life of a stockholder of the corporation
      `the stockholder purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a stockholder's life: is the insurance for the purpose of acquiring at the stockholder's death shares of your stock the stockholder owns?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation have this specific power` IS
    `s 122 the corporation has power` `the power` `the facts`
    WHERE
        `the facts` MEANS `s 122 Facts about the power` WITH
            `the corporation was created under this chapter` IS `my corporation was created under the Law`
            `the certificate of incorporation states a limited period of duration` IS `our certificate states a limited duration`
            `the participation is in a corporation, partnership, limited partnership, joint venture or other association of any kind` IS `the participation is in an association`
            `the participation is in a transaction, undertaking or arrangement` IS `the participation is in a transaction`
            `the participating corporation would have power to conduct the transaction, undertaking or arrangement by itself` IS `we could do it by ourselves`
            `the business is lawful` IS `the business is lawful`
            `the board of directors finds the business to be in aid of governmental authority` IS `the board found it in aid of government`
            `the lending is for the corporation's corporate purposes` IS `the lending is for our corporate purposes`
            `the insurance is for the corporation's benefit` IS `the insurance is for our benefit`
            `whose life is insured` IS `whose life is insured`
            `the insurance on the life of a stockholder is for the purpose of acquiring at the stockholder's death shares of the corporation's stock owned by the stockholder` IS `the stockholder purpose`

-- s 122(5). A contract or delegation that empowers an officer or agent to act for the corporation is subject to s 141(a).
@export Is a contract or delegation that empowers an officer or agent to act for my corporation subject to the board's management power (s 122(5), s 141(a))?
GIVEN `it empowers an officer or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract, appointment or delegation of authority empower an officer or agent to act on behalf of your corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a contract or delegation that empowers an officer or agent to act for my corporation subject to the board's management power` IS
    `s 122(5) the contract, appointment or delegation is subject to section 141(a)` `it empowers an officer or agent`

-- s 122(13). Guaranties for related corporations are deemed necessary or convenient to the business.
@export Is a guaranty my corporation gives for another company within its power as necessary or convenient to its business (s 122(13))?
GIVEN `the other company` IS A `s 122(13) Relationship of the other corporation to the contracting corporation` @desc How is the other company related to your corporation? One of: a corporation all of whose stock your corporation owns (directly or indirectly); a corporation which owns all of your corporation's stock (directly or indirectly); a corporation all of whose stock is owned by a corporation which owns all of your corporation's stock; a person or entity in some other relationship
      `the guaranty is necessary or convenient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the other company is in some other relationship: is the guaranty in fact necessary or convenient to the conduct, promotion or attainment of your corporation's business?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a guaranty my corporation gives for another company within its power as necessary or convenient to its business` IS
    `s 122(13) the contract of guaranty or suretyship is within the power as necessary or convenient to the business of the contracting corporation` `the other company` `the guaranty is necessary or convenient`

-- s 122(17). Renouncing business opportunities.
@export May my corporation renounce an interest or expectancy in business opportunities (s 122(17))?
GIVEN `where we renounce it` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is the interest or expectancy renounced? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in a resolution of the board of directors; in the bylaws; in none of these
      `the opportunities are specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they specified business opportunities, or specified classes or categories of business opportunities?
      `the opportunities are presented to us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they opportunities presented to the corporation or to 1 or more of its officers, directors or stockholders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation renounce an interest or expectancy in business opportunities` IS
    `s 122(17) the corporation may renounce the interest or expectancy` `where we renounce it` `the opportunities are specified` `the opportunities are presented to us`

-- s 122(18). A contract between the corporation and its stockholders: what it may be, and when a provision binds the corporation.
@export May my corporation make this contract with stockholders (s 122(18))?
GIVEN `it is with stockholders as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract made with 1 or more current or prospective stockholders, or beneficial owners of stock, in their capacity as such?
      `the consideration is enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consideration at least the minimum consideration determined by your board of directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation make this contract with stockholders` IF
    `s 122(18) the contract is one the corporation may make with stockholders` `the contract`
    WHERE
        `the contract` MEANS `s 122(18) Facts about the contract` WITH
            `the contract is made with 1 or more current or prospective stockholders, or 1 or more beneficial owners of stock, in its or their capacity as such` IS `it is with stockholders as such`
            `the consideration is at least the minimum consideration determined by the board of directors` IS `the consideration is enough`
            -- Placeholders: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `the provision is contrary to the certificate of incorporation` IS FALSE
            `the provision would be contrary to the laws of this State (other than section 115) if included in the certificate of incorporation` IS FALSE
            `the provision is a restriction, prohibition or covenant that relates to a specified action` IS FALSE
            `the only reason the provision is contrary is a provision of this title or of the certificate of incorporation that authorizes or empowers the board of directors (or any 1 or more directors) to take that action` IS FALSE

-- Answer nothing if it is not a contract of that kind.
@export Can I enforce this provision of my contract with the corporation against it, as a stockholder (s 122(18))?
GIVEN `it is with stockholders as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract made with 1 or more current or prospective stockholders, or beneficial owners of stock, in their capacity as such?
      `the consideration is enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consideration at least the minimum consideration determined by the corporation's board of directors?
      `it is contrary to the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision contrary to the corporation's certificate of incorporation?
      `it would be contrary to the laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the provision be contrary to the laws of Delaware (other than section 115) if it were included in the certificate of incorporation?
      `it restricts a specified action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision a restriction, prohibition or covenant that relates to a specified action?
      `only board powers make it contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only reason it is contrary a provision of the Law or of the certificate that authorizes or empowers the board (or any director) to take that action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I enforce this provision of my contract with the corporation against it, as a stockholder` IS
    `s 122(18) the contract provision is enforceable against the corporation` `the contract`
    WHERE
        `the contract` MEANS `s 122(18) Facts about the contract` WITH
            `the contract is made with 1 or more current or prospective stockholders, or 1 or more beneficial owners of stock, in its or their capacity as such` IS `it is with stockholders as such`
            `the consideration is at least the minimum consideration determined by the board of directors` IS `the consideration is enough`
            `the provision is contrary to the certificate of incorporation` IS `it is contrary to the certificate`
            `the provision would be contrary to the laws of this State (other than section 115) if included in the certificate of incorporation` IS `it would be contrary to the laws`
            `the provision is a restriction, prohibition or covenant that relates to a specified action` IS `it restricts a specified action`
            `the only reason the provision is contrary is a provision of this title or of the certificate of incorporation that authorizes or empowers the board of directors (or any 1 or more directors) to take that action` IS `only board powers make it contrary`

-- Answer nothing for an undertaking of another kind.
@export May my corporation agree to this kind of undertaking in a contract with stockholders (s 122(18))?
GIVEN `the undertaking` IS A `s 122(18) Kind of undertaking` @desc What does the corporation agree to? One of: to restrict or prohibit itself from taking actions specified in the contract; to require the approval or consent of 1 or more persons or bodies before it may take actions specified in the contract; to covenant that it or 1 or more persons or bodies will take, or refrain from taking, actions specified in the contract; an undertaking of any other kind
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation agree to this kind of undertaking in a contract with stockholders` IS
    `s 122(18) the corporation may agree to the undertaking` `the undertaking`

@export Is my corporation subject to the remedies of the law governing a contract it made with stockholders, if it fails to perform (s 122(18))?
GIVEN `it is with stockholders as such` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract made with 1 or more current or prospective stockholders, or beneficial owners of stock, in their capacity as such?
      `the consideration is enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consideration at least the minimum consideration determined by your board of directors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation subject to the remedies of the law governing a contract it made with stockholders, if it fails to perform` IS
    `s 122(18) the corporation is subject to the remedies available under the law governing the contract` `the contract`
    WHERE
        `the contract` MEANS `s 122(18) Facts about the contract` WITH
            `the contract is made with 1 or more current or prospective stockholders, or 1 or more beneficial owners of stock, in its or their capacity as such` IS `it is with stockholders as such`
            `the consideration is at least the minimum consideration determined by the board of directors` IS `the consideration is enough`
            -- Placeholders: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `the provision is contrary to the certificate of incorporation` IS FALSE
            `the provision would be contrary to the laws of this State (other than section 115) if included in the certificate of incorporation` IS FALSE
            `the provision is a restriction, prohibition or covenant that relates to a specified action` IS FALSE
            `the only reason the provision is contrary is a provision of this title or of the certificate of incorporation that authorizes or empowers the board of directors (or any 1 or more directors) to take that action` IS FALSE

-- s 123. Securities of other corporations and entities.
-- Answer nothing for an issuer of a kind the section does not name.
@export May my corporation deal in the securities of another entity in this way (s 123)?
GIVEN `my corporation is organized under the laws of Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation organized under the laws of Delaware?
      `the dealing` IS A `s 123 Kind of dealing` @desc What does your corporation want to do? One of: to guarantee, purchase, take, receive, subscribe for or otherwise acquire; to own, hold, use or otherwise employ; to sell, lease, exchange, transfer or otherwise dispose of; to mortgage, lend, pledge or otherwise deal in and with
      `the issuer` IS A `s 123 Kind of issuer` @desc Who is the issuer? One of: another domestic or foreign corporation; a partnership; an association; an individual; a government or an agency or instrumentality of a government; an issuer of some other kind
      `they are securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they bonds or other obligations of, or shares or other securities or interests in, or issued by, that issuer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation deal in the securities of another entity in this way` IS
    `s 123 the corporation may deal in the securities` `my corporation is organized under the laws of Delaware` `the dealing` `the issuer` `they are securities`

@export May my corporation vote the securities of another entity that it owns, and exercise the other rights of ownership (s 123)?
GIVEN `my corporation owns the securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your corporation own the securities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation vote the securities of another entity that it owns, and exercise the other rights of ownership` IS
    `s 123 the corporation may exercise all the rights, powers and privileges of ownership of the securities, including the right to vote` `my corporation owns the securities`

-- s 124. Lack of corporate capacity or power.
@export Is an act of my corporation, or a conveyance to or by it, invalid because my corporation lacked the capacity or power (s 124)?
GIVEN `my corporation lacked the capacity or power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your corporation without capacity or power to do the act, or to make or receive the conveyance or transfer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an act of my corporation, or a conveyance to or by it, invalid because my corporation lacked the capacity or power` IF
    `s 124 the act, conveyance or transfer is invalid by reason of the corporation's lack of capacity or power` `my corporation lacked the capacity or power`

-- A stockholder suing to enjoin an act, a suit against me as a director or officer, or the Attorney General's suit: yes; any other: no.
@export Can the corporation's lack of capacity or power be asserted in this proceeding (s 124)?
GIVEN `the proceeding` IS A `s 124 Proceeding in which lack of capacity or power is raised` @desc What kind of proceeding is it? One of: a proceeding by a stockholder against the corporation to enjoin the doing of an act or the transfer of property by or to the corporation; a proceeding by the corporation (directly, through a receiver, trustee or other legal representative, or through stockholders in a representative suit) against an incumbent or former officer or director for loss or damage due to an unauthorized act; a proceeding by the Attorney General to dissolve the corporation or to enjoin unauthorized business; a proceeding of any other kind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the corporation's lack of capacity or power be asserted in this proceeding` IF
    `s 124 the lack of capacity or power may be asserted in the proceeding` `the proceeding`

@export May the court set aside and enjoin the performance of a contract of my corporation in a stockholder's suit to enjoin an unauthorized act (s 124(1))?
GIVEN `the acts are performed under a contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the unauthorized acts or transfer sought to be enjoined being, or about to be, performed or made under a contract to which your corporation is a party?
      `all the parties are before the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all of the parties to the contract parties to the proceeding?
      `the court finds it equitable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court deem it equitable to set the contract aside?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court set aside and enjoin the performance of a contract of my corporation in a stockholder's suit to enjoin an unauthorized act` IF
    `s 124(1) the court may set aside and enjoin the performance of the contract` `the acts are performed under a contract` `all the parties are before the court` `the court finds it equitable`

@export May the court award an anticipated profit as a loss or damage sustained when it sets a contract aside (s 124(1))?
GIVEN `the profit is anticipated profit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the loss claimed an anticipated profit to be derived from the performance of the contract?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court award an anticipated profit as a loss or damage sustained when it sets a contract aside` IF
    `s 124(1) the court may award the profit as a loss or damage sustained` `the profit is anticipated profit`

@export May the court allow compensation to my corporation or the other parties for loss from setting the contract aside (s 124(1))?
GIVEN `the court set the contract aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court set aside and enjoined the performance of the contract?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court allow compensation to my corporation or the other parties for loss from setting the contract aside` IS
    `s 124(1) the court may allow compensation for loss or damage resulting from setting aside the contract` `the court set the contract aside`

-- s 125. Degrees; private business or trade schools.
-- Answer nothing if it was organized exactly on 18 April 1945.
@export May my corporation confer academic or honorary degrees (s 125)?
GIVEN `the date my corporation was organized` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your corporation organized? (ISO date, e.g. 1990-06-30)
      `our certificate provides for degrees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation, or an amendment of it, provide that the corporation may confer academic or honorary degrees?
      `the approval was endorsed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the certificate or amendment, before being filed in the office of the Secretary of State, have endorsed on it the approval of the Department of Education of Delaware?
      `we filed the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your corporation was organized before 18 April 1945: have you filed in the office of the Secretary of State a certificate of amendment so providing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation confer academic or honorary degrees` IS
    `s 125 the corporation has power to confer academic or honorary degrees` `the date my corporation was organized` `our certificate provides for degrees` `the approval was endorsed` `we filed the amendment`

-- Answer nothing if the conditions are met (the Law does not say it must approve).
@export Is the Department of Education allowed to approve my corporation's power to confer degrees (s 125)?
GIVEN `it appears we conduct a bona fide institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear, to the reasonable satisfaction of the Department of Education, that your corporation is engaged in conducting a bona fide institution of higher learning, giving instructions in arts and letters, science or the professions?
      `it appears we propose one in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear, to the Department's reasonable satisfaction, that your corporation proposes in good faith to engage in that field and has or will have the resources, including personnel, requisite for an institution of higher learning?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Department of Education allowed to approve my corporation's power to confer degrees` IS
    `s 125 the Department of Education may grant approval` `it appears we conduct a bona fide institution` `it appears we propose one in good faith`

@export Must my corporation comply with section 8530 of Title 14 when it dissolves (s 125)?
GIVEN `my corporation has the power to confer degrees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation one that has power to confer academic or honorary degrees under s 125?
      `my corporation is dissolving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation dissolving?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation comply with section 8530 of Title 14 when it dissolves` IS
    `s 125 the corporation must comply with section 8530 of Title 14` `my corporation has the power to confer degrees` `my corporation is dissolving`

@export May my corporation conduct a private business or trade school (s 125)?
GIVEN `our certificate carries the Department's approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the certificate of incorporation, or an amendment of it, have endorsed on it, before being filed in the office of the Secretary of State, the approval of the Department of Education under Chapter 85 of Title 14?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation conduct a private business or trade school` IF
    `s 125 the corporation has power to conduct a private business or trade school` `our certificate carries the Department's approval`

-- s 125, the law school paragraph.
@export Does my law school corporation have temporary approval from the State (s 125)?
GIVEN `we conduct a law school in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your corporation conduct a law school which has its principal place of operation in Delaware?
      `we intend to meet ABA standards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your corporation intend to meet the standards of approval of the American Bar Association?
      `the date we began actual operation` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your corporation begin actual operation? (ISO date)
      `the date we retained the dean` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your corporation retain the dean or dean emeritus to inspect and report? (ISO date)
      `we retained the dean at our expense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your corporation retain the dean at its own expense to make an on-site inspection and report?
      `the dean is of an ABA approved school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dean or dean emeritus of a law school fully approved by the American Bar Association?
      `the Attorney General chose the dean from the panel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the dean chosen by the Attorney General from a panel of 3 deans nominated one each by your trustees, a committee of the Student Bar Association and a committee of lawyers who are parents of students (with 2 full professors substituted for any dean a group could not find)?
      `the dean reported good faith progress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the dean report in writing that, in the dean's professional judgment, your corporation is attempting in good faith to comply with the ABA standards and is making reasonable progress toward meeting them?
      `we filed the report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your corporation file a copy of the report with the Secretary of Education and with the Attorney General?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my law school corporation have temporary approval from the State` IF
    `s 125 the law school corporation has temporary approval from the State` `my law school`
    WHERE
        `my law school` MEANS `s 125 Facts about a law school corporation` WITH
            `the corporation is conducting a law school which has its principal place of operation in Delaware` IS `we conduct a law school in Delaware`
            `the corporation intends to meet the standards of approval of the American Bar Association` IS `we intend to meet ABA standards`
            `the date the corporation began actual operation` IS `the date we began actual operation`
            `the date the corporation retained the dean` IS `the date we retained the dean`
            `the corporation retained the dean at its own expense to make an on-site inspection and report` IS `we retained the dean at our expense`
            `the dean or dean emeritus is of a law school fully approved by the American Bar Association` IS `the dean is of an ABA approved school`
            `the dean was chosen by the Attorney General from a panel of 3 deans nominated one each by the trustees of the corporation, a committee of the Student Bar Association and a committee of lawyers who are parents of students, with 2 full professors of accredited law schools substituted for any dean a group could not find` IS `the Attorney General chose the dean from the panel`
            `the dean reported in writing that, in the dean's professional judgment, the corporation is attempting, in good faith, to comply with the standards for approval of the American Bar Association and is making reasonable progress toward meeting them` IS `the dean reported good faith progress`
            `the corporation filed a copy of the report with the Secretary of Education and with the Attorney General` IS `we filed the report`

@export Must my law school corporation file a new report this academic year (s 125)?
GIVEN `we have temporary approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your corporation have temporary approval from the State?
      `the ABA has approved our law school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the American Bar Association approved the law school your corporation operates?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my law school corporation file a new report this academic year` IF
    `s 125 the corporation must file a new report once during the academic year` `we have temporary approval` `the ABA has approved our law school`

@export Can the Attorney General sue in the Court of Chancery to suspend my law school corporation's temporary approval and degree-granting power (s 125)?
GIVEN `we have temporary approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your corporation have temporary approval from the State?
      `the ABA has approved our law school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the American Bar Association approved the law school your corporation operates?
      `we failed to file a report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your corporation failed to file a required report?
      `the dean says we are not progressing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the dean retained to render the report state that, in the dean's opinion, your corporation is not continuing to make reasonable progress toward accreditation?
      `the Secretary of Education asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of Education asked the Attorney General to file a complaint?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Attorney General sue in the Court of Chancery to suspend my law school corporation's temporary approval and degree-granting power` IF
    `s 125 the Attorney General may file a complaint in the Court of Chancery to suspend the temporary approval and degree-granting power` `we have temporary approval` `the ABA has approved our law school` `we failed to file a report` `the dean says we are not progressing` `the Secretary of Education asked`

@export Has my law school corporation's temporary approval become final and no longer subject to suspension (s 125)?
GIVEN `the ABA has approved our law school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the American Bar Association approved the law school your corporation operates?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my law school corporation's temporary approval become final and no longer subject to suspension` IF
    `s 125 the temporary approval has become final and is no longer subject to suspension or vacation` `the ABA has approved our law school`

-- s 126. Banking power denied.
-- Answer nothing for any other activity.
@export Does my corporation have the power to issue money-like notes or to take deposits (s 126(a))?
GIVEN `my corporation is organized under the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation organized under the Delaware General Corporation Law?
      `the activity` IS A `s 126(a) Kind of activity` @desc What does your corporation want to do? One of: issuing bills, notes, or other evidences of debt for circulation as money; carrying on the business of receiving deposits of money; any other activity
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation have the power to issue money-like notes or to take deposits` IS
    `s 126(a) the corporation possesses the power` `my corporation is organized under the Law` `the activity`

@export Is my corporation engaging in the business of banking because it deals in notes or lends against collateral (s 126(b))?
GIVEN `we are organized to deal in notes and accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation organized to buy, sell and otherwise deal in notes, open accounts and other similar evidences of debt?
      `we are organized to lend against collateral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation organized to loan money and to take notes, open accounts and other similar evidences of debt as collateral security for the loan?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation engaging in the business of banking because it deals in notes or lends against collateral` IS
    `s 126(b) the corporation is deemed to be engaging in the business of banking` `we are organized to deal in notes and accounts` `we are organized to lend against collateral`

-- s 127. Private foundations.
-- Answer nothing for a tax of any other kind.
@export Must my private foundation act or refrain from acting so as not to incur this federal tax (s 127)?
GIVEN `my corporation is a Delaware corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a corporation of Delaware?
      `my corporation is a private foundation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation a private foundation under the United States internal revenue laws?
      `our certificate opts out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation expressly provide that section 127 shall not apply to it?
      `the tax` IS A `s 127 Tax` @desc Which tax? One of: the 26 U.S.C. section 4941 tax on self-dealing; section 4942 on failure to distribute income; section 4943 on excess business holdings; section 4944 on investments which jeopardize charitable purpose; section 4945 on taxable expenditures; a corresponding provision of a subsequent United States internal revenue law; a tax of any other kind
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my private foundation act or refrain from acting so as not to incur this federal tax` IS
    `s 127 the corporation is required to act or to refrain from acting so as not to subject itself to the tax` `my corporation is a Delaware corporation` `my corporation is a private foundation` `our certificate opts out` `the tax`

§§ `The registered office and the registered agent (ss 131 to 136)`

-- s 131(a), (b), (c). The registered office.
@export Must my corporation have and maintain a registered office in Delaware (s 131(a))?
GIVEN `my corporation is organized under the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation organized under the Delaware General Corporation Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation have and maintain a registered office in Delaware` IS
    `s 131(a) the corporation must have and maintain a registered office in this State` `my corporation is organized under the Law`

@export May my registered office be at a place where my corporation does business in Delaware (s 131(a))?
GIVEN `it is a place of our business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registered office also a place of your corporation's business in Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my registered office be at a place where my corporation does business in Delaware` IF
    `s 131(a) the registered office may be a place of the corporation's business in this State` `it is a place of our business`

-- The address of the registered agent, if it is in Delaware.
@export What is my corporation's registered office (s 131(b))?
GIVEN `my agent's address` IS A STRING @desc What is the address of your corporation's registered agent?
      `the address is in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that address located in Delaware?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `What is my corporation's registered office` IS
    `s 131(b) the registered office` `my agent's address` `the address is in Delaware`

@export Is the address of my registered office, as it appears in a document filed with the Secretary of State, complete (s 131(c))?
GIVEN `it includes the street` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the address include the street?
      `it includes the number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the number?
      `it includes the city` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the city?
      `it includes the county` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the county?
      `it includes the postal code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the postal code?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the address of my registered office, as it appears in a document filed with the Secretary of State, complete` IF
    `s 131(c) the address of the registered office as contained in the filed document is complete` `it includes the street` `it includes the number` `it includes the city` `it includes the county` `it includes the postal code`

-- s 132(a). Who may be the registered agent.
DECLARE `dg2 seat Kind of candidate for registered agent` IS ONE OF
    `an individual, as a candidate for registered agent`
    `a corporation, as a candidate for registered agent`
    `a general partnership, as a candidate for registered agent`
    `a limited partnership, as a candidate for registered agent`
    `a limited liability partnership, as a candidate for registered agent`
    `a limited liability limited partnership, as a candidate for registered agent`
    `a limited liability company, as a candidate for registered agent`
    `a statutory trust, as a candidate for registered agent`
    `a business trust, real estate investment trust, common-law trust, joint-stock association or any other unincorporated business, as a candidate for registered agent`

@export May this person or entity be my corporation's registered agent (s 132(a))?
GIVEN `the candidate is` IS A `dg2 seat Kind of candidate for registered agent` @desc What is the candidate? One of: an individual; a corporation (the corporation itself, another domestic corporation, or a foreign corporation); a general partnership; a limited partnership; a limited liability partnership; a limited liability limited partnership; a limited liability company; a statutory trust; or a business trust, real estate investment trust, common-law trust, joint-stock association or any other unincorporated business
      `the candidate was formed` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law was the candidate formed (not asked for an individual)? One of: this State; another jurisdiction of the United States; a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States
      `the individual lives in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the candidate is an individual: is the individual resident in Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May this person or entity be my corporation's registered agent` IF
    `s 132(a) the candidate may be the registered agent of the corporation` `the kind of candidate` `the candidate was formed` `the individual lives in Delaware`
    WHERE
        -- A corporation is any corporation (the corporation itself, a domestic one, or a foreign one) and the rule does not read its kind.
        `the kind of candidate` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the candidate is`
            WHEN `an individual, as a candidate for registered agent` THEN `a natural person`
            WHEN `a corporation, as a candidate for registered agent` THEN `a corporation` `a stock corporation`
            WHEN `a general partnership, as a candidate for registered agent` THEN `a general partnership`
            WHEN `a limited partnership, as a candidate for registered agent` THEN `a limited partnership`
            WHEN `a limited liability partnership, as a candidate for registered agent` THEN `a limited liability partnership`
            WHEN `a limited liability limited partnership, as a candidate for registered agent` THEN `a limited liability limited partnership`
            WHEN `a limited liability company, as a candidate for registered agent` THEN `a limited liability company`
            WHEN `a statutory trust, as a candidate for registered agent` THEN `a statutory trust`
            WHEN `a business trust, real estate investment trust, common-law trust, joint-stock association or any other unincorporated business, as a candidate for registered agent` THEN `any other unincorporated business or association`

-- s 132(b). What every registered agent must do. The agent's duty is the corporation's claim.
@export Is my corporation's registered agent doing what the Law requires of every registered agent (s 132(b)(1))?
GIVEN `my agent is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your registered agent an individual (not an entity)?
      `my agent keeps an office open` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an entity: does it maintain a business office in Delaware which is generally open at sufficiently frequent times to accept service of process and otherwise perform a registered agent's functions?
      `my agent is generally present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an individual: is it generally present at a designated location in Delaware at sufficiently frequent times to accept service of process and perform a registered agent's functions?
      `my agent is a foreign entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your registered agent a foreign entity?
      `my agent is authorized here` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a foreign entity: is it authorized to transact business in Delaware?
      `my agent accepts and forwards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it accept service of process and other communications directed to the corporations it serves and forward them to the corporation to which they are directed?
      `my agent forwards the annual report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it forward to the corporations it serves the annual report required by section 502 (or an electronic notification of it in a form satisfactory to the Secretary of State)?
      `my agent follows the Secretary's regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it satisfy and adhere to the Secretary of State's regulations on verifying the identity of the entity's contacts and the individuals for which it keeps a record?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation's registered agent doing what the Law requires of every registered agent` IF
    `s 132(b)(1) the registered agent has done what the Law requires of every registered agent` `my agent`
    WHERE
        `my agent` MEANS `s 132(b) Facts about a registered agent` WITH
            `the agent is an individual` IS `my agent is an individual`
            `the agent, an entity, maintains a business office in this State which is generally open at sufficiently frequent times to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent` IS `my agent keeps an office open`
            `the agent, an individual, is generally present at a designated location in this State at sufficiently frequent times to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent` IS `my agent is generally present`
            `the agent is a foreign entity` IS `my agent is a foreign entity`
            `the agent is authorized to transact business in this State` IS `my agent is authorized here`
            `the agent accepts service of process and other communications directed to the corporations it serves and forwards them to the corporation to which the service or communication is directed` IS `my agent accepts and forwards`
            `the agent forwards to the corporations it serves the annual report required by section 502 or an electronic notification of it in a form satisfactory to the Secretary of State` IS `my agent forwards the annual report`
            `the agent satisfies and adheres to the regulations established by the Secretary regarding the verification of the identity of the entity's contacts and the individuals for which the agent maintains a record` IS `my agent follows the Secretary's regulations`

@export May my corporation's registered agent perform its duties in this way (s 132(b)(2))?
GIVEN `it works solely through a virtual office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it perform its duties or functions solely through the internet, or solely through other means of remote communication (a virtual office)?
      `it uses a mail forwarding service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it retain a mail forwarding service?
      `it also works some other way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it perform any of its duties or functions in some other way as well?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation's registered agent perform its duties in this way` IF
    `s 132(b)(2) the registered agent may perform its duties or functions in this way` `it works solely through a virtual office` `it uses a mail forwarding service` `it also works some other way`

-- s 132(c). The commercial registered agent.
@export Is my corporation's registered agent a commercial registered agent (s 132(c))?
GIVEN `the most entities it serves at one time` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest number of entities, domestic or foreign, for which your registered agent serves as registered agent at any one time? (More than 50 makes it a commercial registered agent.)
      `it shares an officer with another agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it have an officer, director or managing agent in common with any other registered agent or agents?
      `the agents it shares with serve together` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what is the greatest number of entities, domestic or foreign, for which those agents together served as registered agents at any time during that common service?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation's registered agent a commercial registered agent` IF
    `s 132(c) the registered agent is a commercial registered agent` `the most entities it serves at one time` `it shares an officer with another agent` `the agents it shares with serve together`

-- An agent that is not a commercial registered agent is not subject to them.
@export Is my corporation's registered agent in compliance with the qualifications for a commercial registered agent (s 132(c))?
GIVEN `the most entities it serves at one time` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the greatest number of entities, domestic or foreign, for which your registered agent serves as registered agent at any one time?
      `it shares an officer with another agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it have an officer, director or managing agent in common with any other registered agent or agents?
      `the agents it shares with serve together` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what is the greatest number of entities for which those agents together served as registered agents at any time during that common service?
      `my agent is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your registered agent a natural person (not an entity)?
      `it lives or works in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a natural person: does it maintain a principal residence or a principal place of business in Delaware?
      `it has an office generally open` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an entity: does it have a business office within Delaware which is generally open during normal business hours to accept service of process and perform a registered agent's functions?
      `it has a Delaware business license` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it maintain a Delaware business license?
      `it is generally present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a natural person: is it generally present at a designated location in Delaware during normal business hours to accept service of process and perform a registered agent's functions?
      `an officer is generally present at its office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is an entity: is an officer, director or managing agent who is a natural person generally present at the office during normal business hours?
      `it gives the Secretary information on request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide the Secretary of State on request with the information identifying and enabling communication with it that the Secretary requires?
      `it follows the Secretary's regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it satisfy and adhere to the Secretary of State's regulations on verifying the identity of the entity's contacts and the individuals for which it keeps a record?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation's registered agent in compliance with the qualifications for a commercial registered agent` IF
    `s 132(c) the registered agent is in compliance with subsection (c)` `it is a commercial registered agent` (`s 132(c) the commercial registered agent meets the qualifications` `its qualifications`)
    WHERE
        `it is a commercial registered agent` MEANS
            `s 132(c) the registered agent is a commercial registered agent` `the most entities it serves at one time` `it shares an officer with another agent` `the agents it shares with serve together`
        `its qualifications` MEANS `s 132(c) Facts about a commercial registered agent` WITH
            `the agent is a natural person` IS `my agent is a natural person`
            `the agent maintains a principal residence or a principal place of business in this State` IS `it lives or works in Delaware`
            `the agent has a business office within this State which is generally open during normal business hours to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent as specified in subsection (b)` IS `it has an office generally open`
            `the agent maintains a Delaware business license` IS `it has a Delaware business license`
            `the agent, a natural person, is generally present at a designated location within this State during normal business hours to accept service of process and otherwise perform the functions of a registered agent as specified in subsection (b)` IS `it is generally present`
            `an officer, director or managing agent who is a natural person is generally present at the office during normal business hours` IS `an officer is generally present at its office`
            `the agent provides the Secretary upon request with the information identifying and enabling communication with the agent that the Secretary requires` IS `it gives the Secretary information on request`
            `the agent satisfies and adheres to the regulations established by the Secretary regarding the verification of the identity of the entity's contacts and the individuals for which it maintains a record` IS `it follows the Secretary's regulations`

-- s 132(d). The communications contact: the corporation's duty, the agent's duty to keep it, the agent's power to resign.
-- Answer nothing for a corporation neither formed nor qualified in Delaware.
@export Has my corporation given its registered agent the communications contact the Law requires (s 132(d))?
GIVEN `we are formed or qualified in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation formed under the laws of Delaware or qualified to do business in Delaware?
      `we gave the contact's name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the registered agent the contact's name?
      `we gave the contact's address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given it the contact's business address?
      `we gave the contact's telephone number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given it the contact's business telephone number?
      `the contact is a natural person of ours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contact a natural person who is an officer, director, employee or designated agent of your corporation?
      `the contact is authorized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person then authorized to receive communications from the registered agent?
      `we keep it up to date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you updated the information from time to time as necessary?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation given its registered agent the communications contact the Law requires` IS
    `s 132(d) the corporation has provided the registered agent with a communications contact as the Law requires` `my contact`
    WHERE
        `my contact` MEANS `s 132(d) Facts about the communications contact` WITH
            `the corporation is formed under the laws of this State or qualified to do business in this State` IS `we are formed or qualified in Delaware`
            `the corporation has provided the registered agent with the name of the person` IS `we gave the contact's name`
            `the corporation has provided the registered agent with the business address of the person` IS `we gave the contact's address`
            `the corporation has provided the registered agent with the business telephone number of the person` IS `we gave the contact's telephone number`
            `the person is a natural person who is an officer, director, employee, or designated agent of the corporation` IS `the contact is a natural person of ours`
            `the person is then authorized to receive communications from the registered agent` IS `the contact is authorized`
            `the corporation has updated the information from time to time as necessary` IS `we keep it up to date`

@export Has my corporation's registered agent kept the information about our communications contact as the Law requires (s 132(d))?
GIVEN `it keeps it on paper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the registered agent keep the information in paper form?
      `it keeps it electronically` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it keep the information in electronic form?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation's registered agent kept the information about our communications contact as the Law requires` IF
    `s 132(d) the registered agent retains the information about the communications contact as the Law requires` `it keeps it on paper` `it keeps it electronically`

@export May my corporation's registered agent resign because we have not given it a current communications contact (s 132(d))?
GIVEN `we have not given a current contact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your corporation failed to provide the registered agent with a current communications contact?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation's registered agent resign because we have not given it a current communications contact` IS
    `s 132(d) the registered agent may resign as the registered agent pursuant to section 136` `we have not given a current contact`

-- s 132(e). The Secretary may refuse to file a document submitted by a registered agent.
-- Answer nothing unless the agent submitted it and refusing is reasonable and necessary to assure compliance.
@export May the Secretary of State refuse to file a document that my registered agent submitted (s 132(e))?
GIVEN `my agent submitted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document submitted by a registered agent?
      `refusing is reasonable and necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is refusing to file it reasonable and necessary to assure the registered agent's compliance with subsections (b), (c) and (d) of section 132?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Secretary of State refuse to file a document that my registered agent submitted` IS
    `s 132(e) the Secretary may refuse to file the document` `my agent submitted it` `refusing is reasonable and necessary`

-- s 132(f). Injunction against a registered agent.
@export May the Court of Chancery enjoin a person or entity from serving as a registered agent, or as an officer, director or managing agent of one (s 132(f))?
GIVEN `the Secretary applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary of State applied to the Court of Chancery?
      `a ground exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a ground exist that is a sufficient basis to grant an injunction (s 132(f)(2))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery enjoin a person or entity from serving as a registered agent, or as an officer, director or managing agent of one` IS
    `s 132(f) the Court of Chancery may enjoin the person or entity from serving` `the Secretary applied` `a ground exists`

-- Answer nothing if the Secretary has filed no complaint.
@export May the Court of Chancery make orders, including interim or final relief, in the Secretary's proceeding against my registered agent or its officers (s 132(f)(1))?
GIVEN `the Secretary filed a complaint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Secretary filed a complaint pursuant to section 132?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court of Chancery make orders, including interim or final relief, in the Secretary's proceeding against my registered agent or its officers` IS
    `s 132(f)(1) the Court may make orders respecting the proceeding and enter orders granting interim or final relief` `the Secretary filed a complaint`

@export Is there a ground on which the Court of Chancery may be asked to enjoin my registered agent or its officers (s 132(f)(2))?
GIVEN `it was a commercial agent within the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the registered agent a commercial registered agent at any time within 1 year before the Secretary's complaint?
      `the latest date it was a commercial agent` IS A DATE @desc If so: what is the latest date on or before the complaint on which it was a commercial registered agent? (ISO date; ignored if not)
      `the date of the complaint` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the Secretary's complaint filed? (ISO date)
      `it failed after a warning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it fail, after notice and warning, to comply with the qualifications in subsection (b) or the requirements of subsection (c) or (d)?
      `a person was convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person serving as registered agent, or an officer, director or managing agent of an entity registered agent, been convicted of a felony or of a crime which includes an element of dishonesty or fraud or involves moral turpitude?
      `it tried to deceive the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the registered agent engaged in conduct, in connection with acting as registered agent, that is intended to or likely to deceive or defraud the public?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is there a ground on which the Court of Chancery may be asked to enjoin my registered agent or its officers` IF
    `s 132(f)(2) a ground exists that is a sufficient basis to grant an injunction` `the grounds`
    WHERE
        `the grounds` MEANS `s 132(f)(2) Facts about the grounds` WITH
            `the latest date on or before the filing of the complaint on which the registered agent was a commercial registered agent` IS (IF `it was a commercial agent within the year` THEN JUST `the latest date it was a commercial agent` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the date the Secretary's complaint was filed` IS `the date of the complaint`
            `the registered agent failed, after notice and warning, to comply with the qualifications in subsection (b) or the requirements of subsection (c) or (d)` IS `it failed after a warning`
            `the person serving as registered agent, or an officer, director or managing agent of an entity registered agent, has been convicted of a felony or of a crime which includes an element of dishonesty or fraud or involves moral turpitude` IS `a person was convicted`
            `the registered agent has engaged in conduct in connection with acting as a registered agent that is intended to or likely to deceive or defraud the public` IS `it tried to deceive the public`

@export Am I, as an officer, director or managing agent of an entity that acts as a registered agent in Delaware, deemed to have consented to service of process in an action under section 132 (s 132(f)(3))?
GIVEN `I serve as an officer, director or managing agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you serve as an officer, director or managing agent of an entity acting as a registered agent in Delaware?
      `the date I serve` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you so serve? (ISO date; on or after 1 January 2007 matters)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I, as an officer, director or managing agent of an entity that acts as a registered agent in Delaware, deemed to have consented to service of process in an action under s 132(f)` IS
    `s 132(f)(3) the person is deemed to have consented to the appointment of the registered agent as agent for service of process` `I serve as an officer, director or managing agent` `the date I serve`

@export May the court direct its order against a registered agent entity to me as a former officer, director or managing agent of it (s 132(f)(3))?
GIVEN `the order concerns an entity that acted as registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order made with respect to an entity that has acted as a registered agent?
      `I served as its officer, director or managing agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you served as an officer, director or managing agent of that registered agent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court direct its order against a registered agent entity to me as a former officer, director or managing agent of it` IS
    `s 132(f)(3) the court may direct the order to the person` `the order concerns an entity that acted as registered agent` `I served as its officer, director or managing agent`

@export By what date must my corporation obtain and designate a new registered agent after the Secretary's notice that the court enjoined our agent (s 132(f)(4))?
GIVEN `where we are formed` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law is your corporation formed? One of: this State; another jurisdiction of the United States; a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States
      `the Secretary sent notice to our address on file` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary mail or deliver notice of the order to your corporation at the address of its principal place of business specified in its most recent franchise tax report or other record of the Secretary?
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given? (ISO date)
      `we designated a new agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you obtained and designated a new registered agent?
      `the date we designated` IS A DATE @desc If so: on what date? (ISO date; ignored if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc As of what date are you asking? (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must my corporation obtain and designate a new registered agent after the Secretary's notice that the court enjoined our agent` IS
    `s 132(f)(4) the last day for the corporation to obtain and designate a new registered agent` `my corporation`
    WHERE
        `my corporation` MEANS `s 132(f)(4) Facts about the corporation` WITH
            `where the corporation is formed` IS `where we are formed`
            `the Secretary mailed or delivered notice of the order to the corporation at the address of its principal place of business specified in its most recent franchise tax report or other record of the Secretary` IS `the Secretary sent notice to our address on file`
            `the date the notice was given` IS `the date of the notice`
            `the date the corporation obtained and designated a new registered agent` IS (IF `we designated a new agent` THEN JUST `the date we designated` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the date as of which the question is asked` IS `today`

-- Answer nothing while the thirty days have not run, or if the Secretary's notice was not given as the subsection requires.
@export What happens to my corporation if the court enjoined its registered agent and we have not designated a new one in the thirty days (s 132(f)(4))?
GIVEN `where we are formed` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law is your corporation formed? One of: this State; another jurisdiction of the United States; a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States
      `the Secretary sent notice to our address on file` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary mail or deliver notice of the order to your corporation at the address of its principal place of business specified in its most recent franchise tax report or other record of the Secretary?
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given? (ISO date)
      `we designated a new agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you obtained and designated a new registered agent?
      `the date we designated` IS A DATE @desc If so: on what date? (ISO date; ignored if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc As of what date are you asking? (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 132 Consequence of failing to designate a new registered agent`
DECIDE `What happens to my corporation if the court enjoined its registered agent and we have not designated a new one in the thirty days` IS
    `s 132(f)(4) what follows for the corporation` `my corporation`
    WHERE
        `my corporation` MEANS `s 132(f)(4) Facts about the corporation` WITH
            `where the corporation is formed` IS `where we are formed`
            `the Secretary mailed or delivered notice of the order to the corporation at the address of its principal place of business specified in its most recent franchise tax report or other record of the Secretary` IS `the Secretary sent notice to our address on file`
            `the date the notice was given` IS `the date of the notice`
            `the date the corporation obtained and designated a new registered agent` IS (IF `we designated a new agent` THEN JUST `the date we designated` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the date as of which the question is asked` IS `today`

@export Is legal process against my corporation to be served on the Secretary of State because the court enjoined its registered agent and no new one was designated (s 132(f)(4))?
GIVEN `the court enjoined our agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court enjoined the person or entity from acting as your corporation's registered agent?
      `we designated a new agent in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a new registered agent obtained and designated in the time and manner required?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is legal process against my corporation to be served on the Secretary of State because the court enjoined its registered agent and no new one was designated` IS
    `s 132(f)(4) service of legal process against the corporation is upon the Secretary` `the court enjoined our agent` `we designated a new agent in time`

-- s 132(h). "Resident agent".
@export Does “resident agent” in my certificate or another document mean the corporation's registered agent (s 132(h))?
GIVEN `the term is a resident agent term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the term “resident agent”, or “resident agent in charge of a corporation's principal office or place of business in this State”, or a term of like import referring to the corporation's agent required by statute to be in Delaware?
      `the context points elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the context indicate otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does “resident agent” in my certificate or another document mean the corporation's registered agent` IS
    `s 132(h) the term is deemed to refer to the corporation's registered agent` `the term is a resident agent term` `the context points elsewhere`

@export Must my corporation amend its certificate of incorporation or another document because it uses the term “resident agent” (s 132(h))?
GIVEN `our documents use the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation or another document use the term “resident agent” or a term of like import?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation amend its certificate of incorporation or another document because it uses the term “resident agent”` IF
    `s 132(h) the corporation must amend its certificate of incorporation or any other document to comply with section 132` `our documents use the term`

-- s 133. Changing the registered office or agent.
@export May my board change the location of our registered office by resolution (s 133)?
GIVEN `the board adopted a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your board of directors adopt a resolution?
      `the new place is in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new place in Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my board change the location of our registered office by resolution` IF
    `s 133 the corporation may change the location of its registered office` `the board adopted a resolution` `the new place is in Delaware`

@export May my board change our registered agent by resolution (s 133)?
GIVEN `the board adopted a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your board of directors adopt a resolution?
      `the new agent is someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new agent a person or corporation other than the present registered agent (it may be the corporation itself)?
      `the new agent is allowed under s 132(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the new agent be a registered agent under section 132(a)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my board change our registered agent by resolution` IF
    `s 133 the corporation may change its registered agent` `the board adopted a resolution` `the new agent is someone else` `the new agent is allowed under s 132(a)`

@export Must my corporation file a certificate certifying the change after our board adopted a resolution changing the registered office or agent (s 133)?
GIVEN `the board adopted a resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your board of directors adopt a resolution changing the registered office or agent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation file a certificate certifying the change after our board adopted a resolution changing the registered office or agent` IS
    `s 133 the corporation must execute, acknowledge and file a certificate certifying the change` `the board adopted a resolution`

@export Has my corporation done what the Law requires after its resolution changing the registered office or agent (s 133)?
GIVEN `the resolution is detailed enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution as detailed in its statement as section 102(a)(2) requires?
      `the certificate was filed properly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate certifying the change executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation done what the Law requires after its resolution changing the registered office or agent` IF
    `s 133 the corporation has done what the Law requires after the resolution` `the resolution is detailed enough` `the certificate was filed properly`

-- s 134. The agent's change of address or name.
-- Answer nothing before the given day or on a defective certificate.
@export Is my corporation's registered office now at the new address that our registered agent certified (s 134(a))?
GIVEN `the person is our registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who filed the certificate your corporation's registered agent?
      `the new address is in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the new address in Delaware?
      `the agent filed a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the registered agent file a certificate with the Secretary of State?
      `the certificate is signed and acknowledged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate executed and acknowledged by the registered agent?
      `the certificate states the old address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth the address at which the agent has maintained the registered office for each corporation it serves?
      `the certificate certifies the new address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it certify the new address to which each registered office will be changed on a given day, at which the agent will thereafter maintain it?
      `the given day` IS A DATE @desc What is the given day? (ISO date)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc As of what date are you asking? (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation's registered office now at the new address that our registered agent certified` IS
    `s 134(a) the registered office of the corporation is located at the new address` `the certificate`
    WHERE
        `the certificate` MEANS `s 134(a) Facts about the registered agent's certificate` WITH
            `the person is the registered agent of the corporation` IS `the person is our registered agent`
            `the new address is in this State` IS `the new address is in Delaware`
            `the registered agent filed a certificate with the Secretary of State` IS `the agent filed a certificate`
            `the certificate is executed and acknowledged by the registered agent` IS `the certificate is signed and acknowledged`
            `the certificate sets forth the address at which the agent has maintained the registered office for each of the corporations for which it is a registered agent` IS `the certificate states the old address`
            `the certificate certifies the new address to which each registered office will be changed on a given day, and at which the agent will thereafter maintain the registered office for each corporation` IS `the certificate certifies the new address`
            `the given day` IS `the given day`
            `the date as of which the question is asked` IS `today`

@export Must our registered agent file a certificate with the Secretary of State because its name changed (s 134(b))?
GIVEN `its name changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the name of the person or corporation acting as your registered agent changed?
      `by a merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it change as a result of a merger or consolidation of the registered agent with or into another person or corporation which succeeds to its assets by operation of law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must our registered agent file a certificate with the Secretary of State because its name changed` IS
    `s 134(b) the registered agent must file a certificate of the change of name` `its name changed` `by a merger or consolidation`

@export Does our registered agent's certificate of the change of name say what the Law requires (s 134(b))?
GIVEN `it is signed and acknowledged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate executed and acknowledged by the registered agent?
      `it gives the new name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth the new name?
      `it gives the old name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth the name before it was changed?
      `it gives the office address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth the address at which the agent has maintained the registered office for each corporation it serves?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our registered agent's certificate of the change of name say what the Law requires` IF
    `s 134(b) the certificate of the change of name says what the Law requires` `it is signed and acknowledged` `it gives the new name` `it gives the old name` `it gives the office address`

-- s 135. Resignation with a successor.
@export Does the successor become my corporation's registered agent, and its address our registered office, when our agent resigns and appoints it (s 135)?
GIVEN `the agent filed the certificate naming the successor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the registered agent file a certificate with the Secretary of State stating the name and address of the successor agent, in accordance with section 102(a)(2)?
      `our statement is attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a statement of your corporation ratifying and approving the change attached to the certificate?
      `our statement is signed and acknowledged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the successor become my corporation's registered agent, and its address our registered office, when our agent resigns and appoints it` IF
    `s 135 the successor becomes the registered agent of the corporation and its address becomes the address of the corporation's registered office` `the agent filed the certificate naming the successor` `our statement is attached` `our statement is signed and acknowledged`

-- s 136. Resignation without a successor.
@export May my corporation's registered agent resign without appointing a successor (s 136(a))?
GIVEN `my corporation has become void` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your corporation become void under section 510 of the Law?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation's registered agent resign without appointing a successor` IF
    `s 136(a) the registered agent may resign without appointing a successor by filing a certificate of resignation` `my corporation has become void`

@export On what date does my registered agent's resignation without a successor take effect (s 136(a))?
GIVEN `the date the certificate of resignation was filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the certificate of resignation filed with the Secretary of State? (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my registered agent's resignation without a successor take effect` IS
    `s 136(a) the date the resignation becomes effective` `the date the certificate of resignation was filed`

@export Is my registered agent's certificate of resignation as the Law requires (s 136(a))?
GIVEN `it is signed and acknowledged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate executed and acknowledged by the registered agent?
      `it states the notice was mailed or delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain a statement that written notice of resignation was given to the corporation by mailing or delivering it at its address last known to the registered agent?
      `it gives the date of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set forth the date of the notice?
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given? (ISO date; at least 30 days before the filing)
      `the date it was filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the certificate filed? (ISO date)
      `it includes our contact information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the information last provided to the registered agent under section 132(d) for our communications contact?
      `it is on the Secretary's form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it on the form prescribed by the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my registered agent's certificate of resignation as the Law requires` IF
    `s 136(a) the certificate of resignation is as the Law requires` `it is signed and acknowledged` `it states the notice was mailed or delivered` `it gives the date of the notice` `the date of the notice` `the date it was filed` `it includes our contact information` `it is on the Secretary's form`

@export Is the information about our communications contact in the certificate of resignation public (s 136(a))?
GIVEN `it is the contact information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information the information regarding the communications contact?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the information about our communications contact in the certificate of resignation public` IF
    `s 136(a) the information regarding the communications contact is deemed public` `it is the contact information`

@export Must my corporation obtain and designate a new registered agent after its agent gave notice of resignation (s 136(b))?
GIVEN `we received the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your corporation received the notice of the resignation of its registered agent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation obtain and designate a new registered agent after its agent gave notice of resignation` IS
    `s 136(b) the corporation must obtain and designate a new registered agent` `we received the notice`

@export By what date must my corporation designate a new registered agent after its agent filed a certificate of resignation (s 136(b))?
GIVEN `where we are formed` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law is your corporation formed? One of: this State; another jurisdiction of the United States; a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States
      `the date the certificate was filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your registered agent file the certificate of resignation? (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must my corporation designate a new registered agent after its agent filed a certificate of resignation` IS
    `s 136(b) the last day for the corporation to obtain and designate a new registered agent` `my corporation`
    WHERE
        `my corporation` MEANS `s 136(b) Facts about the corporation` WITH
            `where the corporation is formed` IS `where we are formed`
            `the date the certificate of resignation was filed` IS `the date the certificate was filed`
            -- Placeholders: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `the date the corporation obtained and designated a new registered agent` IS NOTHING
            `the date as of which the question is asked` IS `the date the certificate was filed`

-- Answer nothing while the thirty days have not run.
@export What happens to my corporation if its registered agent resigned and we did not designate a new one within thirty days (s 136(b))?
GIVEN `where we are formed` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law is your corporation formed? One of: this State; another jurisdiction of the United States; a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States
      `the date the certificate was filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your registered agent file the certificate of resignation? (ISO date)
      `we designated a new agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you obtained and designated a new registered agent?
      `the date we designated` IS A DATE @desc If so: on what date? (ISO date; ignored if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc As of what date are you asking? (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 132 Consequence of failing to designate a new registered agent`
DECIDE `What happens to my corporation if its registered agent resigned and we did not designate a new one within thirty days` IS
    `s 136(b) what follows for the corporation` `my corporation`
    WHERE
        `my corporation` MEANS `s 136(b) Facts about the corporation` WITH
            `where the corporation is formed` IS `where we are formed`
            `the date the certificate of resignation was filed` IS `the date the certificate was filed`
            `the date the corporation obtained and designated a new registered agent` IS (IF `we designated a new agent` THEN JUST `the date we designated` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the date as of which the question is asked` IS `today`

@export Is legal process against my corporation to be served on the Secretary of State because its registered agent resigned and no new one was designated (s 136(c))?
GIVEN `the resignation has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the resignation become effective?
      `we designated a new agent in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a new registered agent obtained and designated in the time and manner required?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is legal process against my corporation to be served on the Secretary of State because its registered agent resigned and no new one was designated` IS
    `s 136(c) service of legal process against the corporation is upon the Secretary of State` `the resignation has taken effect` `we designated a new agent in time`

§§ `The board of directors (s 141)`

-- s 141(a). Who manages.
@export Who manages the business and affairs of my corporation (s 141(a))?
GIVEN `the Law gives the matter to someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the General Corporation Law provide that someone other than the board manages the matter?
      `our certificate gives the matter to someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation provide that someone other than the board manages the matter?
GIVETH A `s 141(a) Who manages the business and affairs`
DECIDE `Who manages the business and affairs of my corporation` IS
    `s 141(a) who manages the business and affairs` `the Law gives the matter to someone else` `our certificate gives the matter to someone else`

-- s 141(b). Members, qualifications, terms and resignation.
@export Does my corporation's board have the one or more members the Law requires (s 141(b))?
GIVEN `the number of members of our board` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does your board of directors have?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation's board have the one or more members the Law requires` IF
    `s 141(b) the board consists of one or more members` `the number of members of our board`

@export May this person be a member of my corporation's board (s 141(b))?
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proposed director a natural person (an individual, not an entity)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May this person be a member of my corporation's board` IF
    `s 141(b) a person of this kind may be a member of the board` `the kind of person`
    WHERE
        -- Any entity other than a natural person gives the same answer: the rule does not read which kind.
        `the kind of person` MEANS IF `the person is a natural person` THEN `a natural person` ELSE `any other unincorporated business or association`

@export How may the number of directors of my corporation be changed (s 141(b))?
GIVEN `our certificate fixes the number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation fix the number of directors?
GIVETH A `s 141(b) How the number of directors is changed`
DECIDE `How may the number of directors of my corporation be changed` IS
    `s 141(b) how the number of directors is changed` `our certificate fixes the number of directors`

@export Must a director of my corporation be a stockholder (s 141(b))?
GIVEN `where the requirement is made` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is the requirement that directors be stockholders made? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must a director of my corporation be a stockholder` IF
    `s 141(b) a director must be a stockholder` `where the requirement is made`

@export Is a qualification for directors, prescribed there, one the Law allows (s 141(b))?
GIVEN `where the qualification is prescribed` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is the qualification prescribed? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a qualification for directors, prescribed there, one the Law allows` IF
    `s 141(b) a qualification for directors prescribed there is one the Law allows` `where the qualification is prescribed`

@export Do I still hold office as a director of my corporation (s 141(b))?
GIVEN `a successor has been elected and qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a successor been elected and qualified?
      `my resignation has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has my resignation become effective?
      `I have been removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have I been removed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I still hold office as a director of my corporation` IF
    `s 141(b) the director still holds office` `a successor has been elected and qualified` `my resignation has taken effect` `I have been removed`

@export Is my notice of resignation as a director in a form the Law allows (s 141(b))?
GIVEN `I gave it to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the notice to the corporation?
      `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice in writing?
      `it is by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give it by electronic transmission?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my notice of resignation as a director in a form the Law allows` IF
    `s 141(b) the notice of resignation is in a form the Law allows` `I gave it to the corporation` `it is in writing` `it is by electronic transmission`

-- Nothing while a date set by an event has not yet come.
@export On what date does my resignation as a director take effect (s 141(b))?
GIVEN `the date I delivered my notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your notice of resignation delivered to the corporation? (ISO date)
      `my notice names a later date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your notice specify a later effective date?
      `the later date` IS A DATE @desc If so: what date? (ISO date; ignored if not)
      `my notice depends on an event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your notice specify an effective date determined upon the happening of an event or events?
      `the event has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: have the event or events happened?
      `the date the event happened` IS A DATE @desc If so: on what date? (ISO date; ignored if not)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my resignation as a director take effect` IS
    `s 141(b) the date the resignation is effective` `my resignation`
    WHERE
        `my resignation` MEANS `s 141(b) Resignation` WITH
            `the date the notice of resignation is delivered to the corporation` IS `the date I delivered my notice`
            `the later effective date the resignation specifies` IS (IF `my notice names a later date` THEN JUST `the later date` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the resignation specifies an effective date determined upon the happening of an event or events` IS `my notice depends on an event`
            `the date the event or events happen` IS (IF `the event has happened` THEN JUST `the date the event happened` ELSE NOTHING)

-- Answer nothing for a resignation not conditioned on failing to receive a vote.
@export May my resignation as a director be made irrevocable (s 141(b))?
GIVEN `my resignation is conditioned on a vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your resignation conditioned upon your failing to receive a specified vote for reelection as a director?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my resignation as a director be made irrevocable` IS
    `s 141(b) the resignation may provide that it is irrevocable` `my resignation is conditioned on a vote`

-- s 141(b). The quorum and the act of the board.
-- Answer nothing where the quorum our instruments fix is not one the Law provides for.
@export Is there a quorum of our board of directors (s 141(b))?
GIVEN `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors are present at the meeting? (Count votes, if the certificate gives a director more or less than one vote.)
      `the total number of directors` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total number of directors on the board? (The full number of seats, vacancies included.)
      `an instrument fixes a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate or the bylaws fix a number of directors as a quorum?
      `the number fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what number? (ignored if not)
      `where it is fixed` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is that number fixed? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
      `our certificate forbids a smaller quorum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation provide that the bylaws may not fix a smaller quorum?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is there a quorum of our board of directors` IS
    `s 141(b) a quorum of the directors is present` `the number of directors present` `our quorum rules`
    WHERE
        `our quorum rules` MEANS `s 141(b) Quorum provisions` WITH
            `the total number of directors` IS `the total number of directors`
            `the number of directors the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws fix as a quorum` IS (IF `an instrument fixes a quorum` THEN JUST `the number fixed` ELSE NOTHING)
            `where that number is fixed` IS `where it is fixed`
            `the certificate of incorporation provides that the bylaws may not fix a smaller quorum` IS `our certificate forbids a smaller quorum`

-- Answer nothing where the quorum is not covered.
@export Did our board of directors carry the act at this meeting (s 141(b))?
GIVEN `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors were present? (Count votes, if the certificate gives a director more or less than one vote.)
      `the number voting in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voted in favor?
      `the total number of directors` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total number of directors on the board? (The full number of seats, vacancies included.)
      `an instrument fixes a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate or the bylaws fix a number of directors as a quorum?
      `the number fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what number? (ignored if not)
      `where it is fixed` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is that number fixed? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
      `our certificate forbids a smaller quorum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation provide that the bylaws may not fix a smaller quorum?
      `where a greater vote is required` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is a vote of a greater number required? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
      `the greater number required` IS A NUMBER @desc If a greater vote is required: how many directors must vote in favor? (ignored if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did our board of directors carry the act at this meeting` IS
    `s 141(b) the act of the board of directors is carried` `our quorum rules` `our vote`
    WHERE
        `our quorum rules` MEANS `s 141(b) Quorum provisions` WITH
            `the total number of directors` IS `the total number of directors`
            `the number of directors the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws fix as a quorum` IS (IF `an instrument fixes a quorum` THEN JUST `the number fixed` ELSE NOTHING)
            `where that number is fixed` IS `where it is fixed`
            `the certificate of incorporation provides that the bylaws may not fix a smaller quorum` IS `our certificate forbids a smaller quorum`
        `our vote` MEANS `s 141(b) Vote of the board` WITH
            `the number of directors present at the meeting` IS `the number of directors present`
            `the number of directors voting in favor` IS `the number voting in favor`
            `where a vote of a greater number is required` IS `where a greater vote is required`
            `the greater number of directors required to vote in favor` IS `the greater number required`

-- s 141(j). A nonstock corporation.
@export May the certificate of my nonstock corporation set a quorum of less than one third of the governing body (s 141(j))?
GIVEN `my kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is yours? One of: a stock corporation; a nonstock corporation with membership interests; a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable; a charitable nonstock corporation
      `where the smaller quorum is provided` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is the smaller quorum provided? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the certificate of my nonstock corporation set a quorum of less than one third of the governing body` IF
    `s 141(j) a quorum of less than one third of the members of the governing body may be provided` `my kind of corporation` `where the smaller quorum is provided`

@export May the business and affairs of my nonstock corporation be managed in a manner different from that provided in section 141 (s 141(j))?
GIVEN `my kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is yours? One of: a stock corporation; a nonstock corporation with membership interests; a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable; a charitable nonstock corporation
      `where the different manner is provided` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is the different manner of management provided? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the business and affairs of my nonstock corporation be managed in a manner different from that provided in section 141` IF
    `s 141(j) the business and affairs may be managed in a different manner` `my kind of corporation` `where the different manner is provided`

-- Answer nothing for a stock corporation or where our certificate provides otherwise.
@export How is a reference in section 141 to the board, to a director, to stockholders or to stock read for my nonstock corporation (s 141(j))?
GIVEN `the reference` IS A `s 141(j) Reference in section 141` @desc Which reference? One of: a reference in section 141 to the board of directors; to a member of the board of directors; to stockholders; to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof
      `my kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is yours? One of: a stock corporation; a nonstock corporation with membership interests; a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable; a charitable nonstock corporation
      `our certificate provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation provide otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 141(j) How a reference is read for a nonstock corporation`
DECIDE `How is a reference in section 141 to the board, to a director, to stockholders or to stock read for my nonstock corporation` IS
    `s 141(j) how a reference in section 141 is read` `the reference` `my kind of corporation` `our certificate provides otherwise`

§§ `Committees of the board (s 141(c))`

-- Answer nothing if the resolution's votes cannot be a vote.
@export Which paragraph of s 141(c) governs the committees of my corporation (s 141(c))?
GIVEN `the date we were incorporated` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your corporation incorporated? (ISO date; before 1 July 1996 matters)
      `the number of directors on the whole board` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors are there on the whole board?
      `we adopted a resolution electing paragraph (c)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your board adopt a resolution electing to be governed by paragraph (c)(2)?
      `the number of the whole board who adopted it` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: how many of the whole board voted for it? (ignored if no resolution)
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 141(c) Paragraph that governs the corporation`
DECIDE `Which paragraph of s 141(c) governs the committees of my corporation` IS
    `s 141(c) which paragraph governs the corporation` `the date we were incorporated` `the number of directors on the whole board` (IF `we adopted a resolution electing paragraph (c)(2)` THEN JUST `the number of the whole board who adopted it` ELSE NOTHING)

@export May our board designate this committee, as a corporation governed by paragraph (c)(1) (s 141(c)(1))?
GIVEN `the number of directors on the whole board` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors are there on the whole board?
      `the number of the whole board who passed the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the whole board passed the resolution designating the committee?
      `the number of directors on the committee` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors does the committee consist of?
      `all its members are directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is every member of the committee a director of the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our board designate this committee, as a corporation governed by paragraph (c)(1)` IS
    `s 141(c)(1) the board may designate the committee` `the number of directors on the whole board` `the number of the whole board who passed the resolution` `the number of directors on the committee` `all its members are directors`

@export May our board designate this committee, as a corporation governed by paragraph (c)(2) (s 141(c)(2))?
GIVEN `the board acted by the vote section 141(b) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board act by the vote that section 141(b) requires?
      `the number of directors on the committee` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors does the committee consist of?
      `all its members are directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is every member of the committee a director of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our board designate this committee, as a corporation governed by paragraph (c)(2)` IF
    `s 141(c)(2) the board may designate the committee` `the board acted by the vote section 141(b) requires` `the number of directors on the committee` `all its members are directors`

@export May an alternate member replace a committee member at this meeting (s 141(c))?
GIVEN `the board designated the alternate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board designate the person as an alternate member of the committee?
      `the alternate is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director of the corporation?
      `the member is absent or disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the member absent or disqualified?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May an alternate member replace a committee member at this meeting` IF
    `s 141(c) an alternate member may replace the member at the meeting` `the board designated the alternate` `the alternate is a director` `the member is absent or disqualified`

@export May the members present appoint another director to act at the committee meeting in place of an absent member (s 141(c))?
GIVEN `our bylaws so provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your bylaws so provide?
      `the members present agree unanimously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the members present at the meeting and not disqualified from voting appoint unanimously, whether or not they constitute a quorum?
      `the appointee is on the board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person appointed a member of the board of directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the members present appoint another director to act at the committee meeting in place of an absent member` IF
    `s 141(c) the members present may appoint another director to act in place of the absent member` `our bylaws so provide` `the members present agree unanimously` `the appointee is on the board`

-- Answer nothing where paragraph (c)(1) does not say.
@export Does our committee have the power to act in this matter (s 141(c))?
GIVEN `the paragraph that governs` IS A `s 141(c) Paragraph that governs the corporation` @desc Which paragraph governs your corporation? One of: paragraph (c)(1) of section 141 governs the corporation; paragraph (c)(2) of section 141 governs the corporation
      `the matter` IS A `s 141(c) Matter before a committee` @desc What is the matter? One of: amending the certificate of incorporation (other than fixing share terms under a s 151(a) resolution); fixing share terms or the number of shares of a series under a resolution adopted as provided in s 151(a); adopting a merger or consolidation agreement under s 251, 252, 254, 255, 256, 257, 258, 263 or 264; adopting one under another section; recommending to stockholders a sale, lease or exchange of all or substantially all assets; recommending a dissolution or revocation; amending, adopting or repealing a bylaw; declaring a dividend; authorizing the issuance of stock; adopting a s 253 certificate of ownership and merger; approving or recommending to stockholders a matter this chapter requires them to approve; approving or recommending the election or removal of directors; any other matter
      `the board or bylaws gave the committee the board's power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution of the board of directors, or the bylaws, provide that the committee has and may exercise the power of the board?
      `an instrument expressly gave this power` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the resolution, the bylaws or the certificate expressly provide that the committee may do this thing?
      `it acts within the s 151(a) resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the committee act to the extent authorized in a resolution providing for the issuance of shares adopted by the board as provided in section 151(a)?
      `the chapter requires stockholders to approve it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the General Corporation Law expressly require the matter to be submitted to stockholders for approval?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our committee have the power to act in this matter` IS
    `s 141(c) the committee has the power in the matter` `the paragraph that governs` `the matter` `what we gave it`
    WHERE
        `what we gave it` MEANS `s 141(c) What the board or the bylaws gave the committee` WITH
            `the resolution of the board of directors or the bylaws provide that the committee has and may exercise the power of the board` IS `the board or bylaws gave the committee the board's power`
            `the resolution, the bylaws or the certificate of incorporation expressly provide that the committee may do the thing` IS `an instrument expressly gave this power`
            `the committee acts to the extent authorized in a resolution providing for the issuance of shares adopted by the board as provided in s 151(a)` IS `it acts within the s 151(a) resolution`
            `this chapter expressly requires the matter to be submitted to stockholders for approval` IS `the chapter requires stockholders to approve it`

@export May our committee create a subcommittee and delegate its powers to it (s 141(c)(3))?
GIVEN `where it is otherwise provided` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Is it otherwise provided in the certificate, the bylaws or the board's resolution designating the committee? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
      `the number of committee members on the subcommittee` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members of the committee does the subcommittee consist of?
      `all of them are on the committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is every member of the subcommittee a member of the committee?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our committee create a subcommittee and delegate its powers to it` IF
    `s 141(c)(3) the committee may create the subcommittee and delegate its powers to it` `where it is otherwise provided` `the number of committee members on the subcommittee` `all of them are on the committee`

@export Does a reference in the Law to a committee of the board include a subcommittee (s 141(c)(3))?
GIVEN `the reference is in subsection (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference inside subsection (c) of section 141?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a reference in the Law to a committee of the board include a subcommittee` IF
    `s 141(c)(3) a reference to a committee includes a subcommittee` `the reference is in subsection (c)`

-- Answer nothing where the number fixed is below one third of those serving or above their number.
@export Is there a quorum of our committee or subcommittee (s 141(c)(4))?
GIVEN `the number of members present` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members are present?
      `the number serving` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors are then serving on the committee or subcommittee?
      `a number is fixed as a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate, the bylaws, a resolution of the board or a resolution of the committee that created the subcommittee fix a number as a quorum?
      `the number fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what number? (ignored if not)
      `where the quorum is fixed` IS A `s 141(c)(4) Where the committee's number is fixed` @desc Where is it fixed? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in a resolution of the committee that created the subcommittee; in none of these (the choices are named “for a committee under s 141(c)(4)”)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is there a quorum of our committee or subcommittee` IS
    `s 141(c)(4) a quorum of the committee is present` `the number of members present` `our committee rules`
    WHERE
        `our committee rules` MEANS `s 141(c)(4) Committee provisions` WITH
            `the number of directors then serving on the committee or subcommittee` IS `the number serving`
            `the number fixed as a quorum` IS (IF `a number is fixed as a quorum` THEN JUST `the number fixed` ELSE NOTHING)
            `where the quorum is fixed` IS `where the quorum is fixed`
            -- Placeholders: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `the number of members who must vote in favor, if a greater number is fixed` IS NOTHING
            `where the greater vote is fixed` IS `in none of these, for a committee under s 141(c)(4)`

@export Did our committee or subcommittee carry the act at this meeting (s 141(c)(4))?
GIVEN `the number of members present` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members were present?
      `the number voting in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many voted in favor?
      `the number serving` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors are then serving on the committee or subcommittee?
      `a number is fixed as a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the certificate, the bylaws, a resolution of the board or a resolution of the committee that created the subcommittee fix a number as a quorum?
      `the number fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what number? (ignored if not)
      `where the quorum is fixed` IS A `s 141(c)(4) Where the committee's number is fixed` @desc Where is it fixed? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in a resolution of the committee that created the subcommittee; in none of these (the choices are named “for a committee under s 141(c)(4)”)
      `a greater vote is fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do those instruments require a vote of a greater number?
      `the greater number` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: how many members must vote in favor? (ignored if not)
      `where the greater vote is fixed` IS A `s 141(c)(4) Where the committee's number is fixed` @desc Where is that fixed? (same choices)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did our committee or subcommittee carry the act at this meeting` IS
    `s 141(c)(4) the act of the committee is carried` `the number of members present` `the number voting in favor` `our committee rules`
    WHERE
        `our committee rules` MEANS `s 141(c)(4) Committee provisions` WITH
            `the number of directors then serving on the committee or subcommittee` IS `the number serving`
            `the number fixed as a quorum` IS (IF `a number is fixed as a quorum` THEN JUST `the number fixed` ELSE NOTHING)
            `where the quorum is fixed` IS `where the quorum is fixed`
            `the number of members who must vote in favor, if a greater number is fixed` IS (IF `a greater vote is fixed` THEN JUST `the greater number` ELSE NOTHING)
            `where the greater vote is fixed` IS `where the greater vote is fixed`

§§ `Classes of directors, reliance, action without a meeting, meetings, removal (s 141(d) to (k))`

@export May the directors of my corporation be divided into classes by this instrument (s 141(d))?
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `s 141(d) Instrument that classifies the board` @desc What instrument divides them? One of: the certificate of incorporation; an initial bylaw; a bylaw adopted by a vote of the stockholders; a bylaw adopted by the directors alone (the choices are named “under s 141(d)”)
      `the number of classes` IS A NUMBER @desc Into how many classes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors of my corporation be divided into classes by this instrument` IF
    `s 141(d) the directors may be divided into classes by the instrument` `the instrument` `the number of classes`

-- Nothing for a class other than the first, second or third.
@export On what date does the term of my class of directors expire (s 141(d))?
GIVEN `my class` IS A NUMBER @desc Which class are you in (1, 2 or 3)?
      `the date of the first annual meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the first annual meeting held after the classification became effective? (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what date does the term of my class of directors expire` IS
    `s 141(d) the date the term of the class expires` `my class` `the date of the first annual meeting`

-- Answer nothing if the provision dividing the directors does not authorize it.
@export May our board assign the directors already in office to the classes (s 141(d))?
GIVEN `the provision authorizes the board to assign them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate or bylaw provision dividing the directors into classes authorize the board to assign members already in office to the classes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our board assign the directors already in office to the classes` IS
    `s 141(d) the board may assign the directors in office to the classes` `the provision authorizes the board to assign them`

@export May the holders of a class or series of our stock be given the right to elect directors in this way (s 141(d))?
GIVEN `where the right is conferred` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is the right conferred? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the holders of a class or series of our stock be given the right to elect directors in this way` IF
    `s 141(d) the holders of a class or series of stock may be given the right to elect directors` `where the right is conferred`

@export May a director of my corporation be given greater or lesser voting power than the other directors in this way (s 141(d))?
GIVEN `where the voting power is conferred` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is the greater or lesser voting power conferred? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a director of my corporation be given greater or lesser voting power than the other directors in this way` IF
    `s 141(d) a director may be given greater or lesser voting power than other directors` `where the voting power is conferred`

@export Does a director's greater or lesser voting power apply to voting in a committee (s 141(d))?
GIVEN `where it is otherwise provided` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Is it otherwise provided in the certificate or the bylaws? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a director's greater or lesser voting power apply to voting in a committee` IF
    `s 141(d) the greater or lesser voting power applies to voting in a committee` `where it is otherwise provided`

@export Do the Law's references to a majority or other proportion of the directors count the directors' votes in my corporation (s 141(d))?
GIVEN `our certificate gives a director more or less than one vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your certificate of incorporation provide that 1 or more directors have more or less than 1 vote per director on any matter?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the Law's references to a majority or other proportion of the directors count the directors' votes in my corporation` IF
    `s 141(d) a majority or other proportion of the directors is a proportion of the votes of the directors` `our certificate gives a director more or less than one vote`

@export Am I fully protected, as a director or committee member, in relying on this record or report (s 141(e))?
GIVEN `I am a director or committee member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the board of directors, or of a committee designated by it?
      `I relied in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you rely in good faith?
      `what I relied on` IS A `s 141(e) What the member relied on` @desc What did you rely on? One of: the records of the corporation; information, opinions, reports or statements presented to the corporation by an officer or employee; the same by a committee of the board; the same by any other person
      `I believed it was within the person's expertise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was any other person: did you reasonably believe the matter was within that person's professional or expert competence?
      `the person was selected with care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was any other person: was that person selected with reasonable care by or on behalf of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I fully protected, as a director or committee member, in relying on this record or report` IF
    `s 141(e) the member is fully protected in relying` `I am a director or committee member` `I relied in good faith` `what I relied on` `I believed it was within the person's expertise` `the person was selected with care`

@export May our board or committee act without a meeting (s 141(f))?
GIVEN `the number of members` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does the board or committee have?
      `the number who consent` IS A NUMBER @desc How many consent in writing or by electronic transmission?
      `the consents are documented under s 116` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the consents documented, signed and delivered in a manner permitted by section 116?
      `where the restriction is made` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Is action without a meeting restricted? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our board or committee act without a meeting` IF
    `s 141(f) the board or committee may act without a meeting` `the number of members` `the number who consent` `the consents are documented under s 116` `where the restriction is made`

@export Is my consent, effective at a future time, deemed given at that time (s 141(f))?
GIVEN `the date I gave the instruction` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you give the instruction, or make the provision, that the consent would be effective later? (ISO date)
      `the date it is to be effective` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the consent to take effect? (ISO date; no later than 60 days after)
      `I am a director at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you then be a director?
      `I revoked it before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you revoke the consent before that time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my consent, effective at a future time, deemed given at that time` IF
    `s 141(f) the consent is deemed given at its effective time` `the date I gave the instruction` `the date it is to be effective` `I am a director at that time` `I revoked it before`

-- Answer nothing once it has become effective.
@export May I still revoke my consent to board action without a meeting (s 141(f))?
GIVEN `my consent has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the consent become effective?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I still revoke my consent to board action without a meeting` IS
    `s 141(f) the consent may be revoked` `my consent has become effective`

@export Have the consents been filed as the Law requires after the board's action (s 141(f))?
GIVEN `they are filed with the minutes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the consents filed with the minutes of the proceedings of the board or committee?
      `they are in the same form as the minutes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they filed in the same paper or electronic form as the minutes are maintained?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the consents been filed as the Law requires after the board's action` IF
    `s 141(f) the consents have been filed as the Law requires` `they are filed with the minutes` `they are in the same form as the minutes`

@export May our board hold its meetings, and have an office, outside Delaware (s 141(g))?
GIVEN `where the restriction is made` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Is this restricted? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our board hold its meetings, and have an office, outside Delaware` IF
    `s 141(g) the board may hold its meetings, and have an office or offices, outside this State` `where the restriction is made`

@export Does our board have the authority to fix the compensation of directors (s 141(h))?
GIVEN `where the restriction is made` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Is this restricted? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our board have the authority to fix the compensation of directors` IF
    `s 141(h) the board has the authority to fix the compensation of directors` `where the restriction is made`

@export Does my participation in a board meeting by telephone count as being present in person (s 141(i))?
GIVEN `I take part by conference telephone or other equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you participate by conference telephone or other communications equipment?
      `everyone can hear everyone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can all persons participating in the meeting hear each other?
      `where the restriction is made` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Is this restricted? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my participation in a board meeting by telephone count as being present in person` IF
    `s 141(i) the participation constitutes presence in person at the meeting` `I take part by conference telephone or other equipment` `everyone can hear everyone` `where the restriction is made`

-- Answer nothing where the share counts cannot be a vote.
@export May the stockholders remove this director from office (s 141(k))?
GIVEN `the removal is for cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the removal for cause?
      `the board is classified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the board classified as provided in subsection (d)?
      `our certificate allows removal without cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate provide that stockholders may remove a classified board without cause?
      `we have cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have cumulative voting?
      `less than the entire board is to be removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is less than the entire board to be removed?
      `the votes against would elect the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the votes cast against the removal be sufficient to elect the director if then cumulatively voted at an election of the entire board (or of the director's class)?
      `elected by a class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the director elected by the holders of a class or series of stock under the certificate?
      `shares entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares are then entitled to vote at an election of directors?
      `shares voted for removal` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them voted for removal?
      `class shares entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc If the director was elected by a class or series: how many shares of that class or series are then entitled to vote?
      `class shares voted for removal` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them voted for removal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the stockholders remove this director from office` IS
    `s 141(k) the stockholders may remove the director` `the removal`
    WHERE
        `the removal` MEANS `s 141(k) Removal` WITH
            `the removal is for cause` IS `the removal is for cause`
            `the board is classified as provided in subsection (d)` IS `the board is classified`
            `the certificate of incorporation provides that stockholders may remove a classified board without cause` IS `our certificate allows removal without cause`
            `the corporation has cumulative voting` IS `we have cumulative voting`
            `less than the entire board is to be removed` IS `less than the entire board is to be removed`
            `the votes cast against the removal would be sufficient to elect the director if then cumulatively voted` IS `the votes against would elect the director`
            `the director was elected by the holders of a class or series of stock under the certificate of incorporation` IS `elected by a class or series`
            `the number of shares then entitled to vote at an election of directors` IS `shares entitled to vote`
            `the number of those shares voted in favor of removal` IS `shares voted for removal`
            `the number of shares of the class or series then entitled to vote` IS `class shares entitled to vote`
            `the number of those shares voted in favor of removal, of the class or series` IS `class shares voted for removal`

§§ `Officers and loans to them (ss 142 and 143)`

-- Answer nothing if they are stated only in the certificate.
@export Are the titles and duties of my corporation's officers stated as the Law requires (s 142(a))?
GIVEN `where they are stated` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where are the officers' titles and duties stated? One of: in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in the certificate of incorporation; in none of these
      `the resolution contradicts the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If in a resolution of the board: is it inconsistent with the bylaws?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the titles and duties of my corporation's officers stated as the Law requires` IS
    `s 142(a) the titles and duties of the officers are stated as the Law requires` `where they are stated` `the resolution contradicts the bylaws`

@export Does my corporation have the officers it needs to sign instruments and stock certificates (s 142(a))?
GIVEN `our officers are enough to sign` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your officers enough to enable the corporation to sign the instruments and stock certificates which comply with sections 103(a)(2) and 158?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation have the officers it needs to sign instruments and stock certificates` IF
    `s 142(a) the corporation has the officers it needs to sign instruments and stock certificates` `our officers are enough to sign`

@export Does one of my corporation's officers have the duty to record the proceedings of the meetings of stockholders and directors (s 142(a))?
GIVEN `the officers who record the proceedings` IS A NUMBER @desc How many officers have the duty to record the proceedings of the meetings of the stockholders and directors in a book kept for that purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does one of my corporation's officers have the duty to record the proceedings of the meetings of stockholders and directors` IF
    `s 142(a) one of the officers has the duty to record the proceedings of the meetings` `the officers who record the proceedings`

@export May one person hold any number of offices in my corporation (s 142(a))?
GIVEN `where it is otherwise provided` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Do the certificate or the bylaws otherwise provide? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May one person hold any number of offices in my corporation` IF
    `s 142(a) the same person may hold any number of offices` `where it is otherwise provided`

@export Are my corporation's officers chosen, and their terms fixed, as the Law provides (s 142(b))?
GIVEN `the bylaws prescribe it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the manner of choosing the officers and their terms prescribed by the bylaws?
      `the board determines it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they determined by the board of directors or other governing body?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my corporation's officers chosen, and their terms fixed, as the Law provides` IF
    `s 142(b) the manner of choosing the officers and their terms are fixed as the Law provides` `the bylaws prescribe it` `the board determines it`

@export Do I still hold office as an officer of my corporation (s 142(b))?
GIVEN `a successor has been elected and qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a successor been elected and qualified?
      `I have resigned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you resigned?
      `I have been removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been removed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I still hold office as an officer of my corporation` IF
    `s 142(b) the officer still holds office` `a successor has been elected and qualified` `I have resigned` `I have been removed`

-- Answer nothing if you do not give written notice (the Law names no other way).
@export May I resign as an officer of my corporation (s 142(b))?
GIVEN `I gave written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give written notice of the resignation to the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I resign as an officer of my corporation` IS
    `s 142(b) the officer may resign` `I gave written notice`

@export May my corporation secure the fidelity of this person by bond or otherwise (s 142(c))?
GIVEN `the person is an officer or agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer or an agent of the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation secure the fidelity of this person by bond or otherwise` IS
    `s 142(c) the corporation may secure the fidelity of the person by bond or otherwise` `the person is an officer or agent`

@export Does my corporation's failure to elect officers dissolve it or otherwise affect it (s 142(d))?
GIVEN `we have not elected officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation failed to elect officers?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation's failure to elect officers dissolve it or otherwise affect it` IF
    `s 142(d) the failure to elect officers dissolves or otherwise affects the corporation` `we have not elected officers`

@export Who fills a vacancy in an office of my corporation (s 142(e))?
GIVEN `the bylaws say how` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the bylaws provide how a vacancy is to be filled?
GIVETH A `s 142(e) Who fills a vacancy`
DECIDE `Who fills a vacancy in an office of my corporation` IS
    `s 142(e) how the vacancy in the office is filled` `the bylaws say how`

@export May my corporation lend me money, guarantee my obligation or otherwise assist me, as an officer or employee (s 143)?
GIVEN `I am an officer or employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an officer or other employee of the corporation or of its subsidiary (a director of either included)?
      `the directors judge it will benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the judgment of the directors, may the loan, guaranty or assistance reasonably be expected to benefit the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation lend me money, guarantee my obligation or otherwise assist me, as an officer or employee` IF
    `s 143 the corporation may lend money to, guarantee an obligation of, or otherwise assist the person` `I am an officer or employee` `the directors judge it will benefit`

@export May a loan, guaranty or other assistance to an officer or employee be with or without interest (s 143)?
GIVEN `the loan bears interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it bear interest?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a loan, guaranty or other assistance to an officer or employee be with or without interest` IF
    `s 143 the loan, guaranty or other assistance may be with or without interest` `the loan bears interest`

@export May a loan, guaranty or other assistance to an officer or employee be secured in this way (s 143)?
GIVEN `the security` IS A `s 143 How the loan is secured` @desc How is it secured? One of: unsecured; secured in a manner the board of directors approves; secured by a pledge of shares of stock of the corporation, a manner the board of directors approves; secured in a manner the board of directors has not approved
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a loan, guaranty or other assistance to an officer or employee be secured in this way` IF
    `s 143 the loan, guaranty or other assistance may be secured in this way` `the security`

@export Does section 143 limit my corporation's powers of guaranty or warranty at common law or under a statute (s 143)?
GIVEN `it is a power the corporation has elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the power of guaranty or warranty one the corporation has at common law or under a statute?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 143 limit my corporation's powers of guaranty or warranty at common law or under a statute` IF
    `s 143 this section denies, limits or restricts the power` `it is a power the corporation has elsewhere`

§§ `Interested directors and officers; controlling stockholders (s 144)`

-- The vote of the disinterested stockholders, asked in the same words by (a), (b) and (c).
@export How many votes are counted as cast, and as cast in favor, when disinterested stockholders' shares are tendered in an offer under section 251(h) (s 144(d)(7))?
GIVEN `it is a section 251(h) offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act or transaction an offer contemplated by section 251(h)?
      `votes cast` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is not: how many votes did the disinterested stockholders cast?
      `votes cast in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is not: how many of those votes were in favor?
      `shares irrevocably accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is: how many shares have been irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer?
      `disinterested shares not accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc If it is: how many shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders have not been irrevocably accepted?
GIVETH A `s 144(d)(7) Votes counted`
DECIDE `How many votes are counted as cast, and as cast in favor, when disinterested stockholders' shares are tendered in an offer under section 251(h)` IS
    `s 144(d)(7) the votes counted` `the stockholder vote`
    WHERE
        `the stockholder vote` MEANS `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders` WITH
            `the act or transaction is an offer contemplated by section 251(h)` IS `it is a section 251(h) offer`
            `the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders` IS `votes cast`
            `the votes cast in favor by the disinterested stockholders` IS `votes cast in favor`
            `the number of shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS `shares irrevocably accepted`
            `the number of shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders not irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS `disinterested shares not accepted`
            -- Placeholders: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `the vote was informed` IS TRUE
            `the vote was uncoerced` IS TRUE

@export Did the disinterested stockholders approve or ratify the act or transaction by an informed, uncoerced, affirmative vote of a majority of the votes cast (s 144(a)(2))?
GIVEN `it is a section 251(h) offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act or transaction an offer contemplated by section 251(h)?
      `the vote was informed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vote informed?
      `the vote was uncoerced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vote uncoerced?
      `votes cast` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes did the disinterested stockholders cast? (ignored for a section 251(h) offer)
      `votes cast in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those votes were in favor? (ignored for a section 251(h) offer)
      `shares irrevocably accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc For a section 251(h) offer: how many shares have been irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange?
      `disinterested shares not accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc For a section 251(h) offer: how many shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders have not been irrevocably accepted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the disinterested stockholders approve or ratify the act or transaction by an informed, uncoerced, affirmative vote of a majority of the votes cast` IS
    `s 144(a)(2) the disinterested stockholders approved or ratified by an informed, uncoerced, affirmative vote of a majority of the votes cast` `the stockholder vote`
    WHERE
        `the stockholder vote` MEANS `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders` WITH
            `the act or transaction is an offer contemplated by section 251(h)` IS `it is a section 251(h) offer`
            `the vote was informed` IS `the vote was informed`
            `the vote was uncoerced` IS `the vote was uncoerced`
            `the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders` IS `votes cast`
            `the votes cast in favor by the disinterested stockholders` IS `votes cast in favor`
            `the number of shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS `shares irrevocably accepted`
            `the number of shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders not irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS `disinterested shares not accepted`

@export Did the disinterested directors authorize the act or transaction as the Law requires (s 144(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the facts were disclosed or known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the material facts as to the director's or officer's relationship or interest and as to the act or transaction disclosed or known to all members of the board or committee?
      `the body acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board or committee authorize the act or transaction in good faith?
      `the body was not grossly negligent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it do so without gross negligence?
      `disinterested directors serving` IS A NUMBER @desc How many disinterested directors were then serving on the board or on the committee that authorized it?
      `disinterested directors in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them voted in favor?
      `directors on the board` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors were then serving on the board?
      `disinterested directors on the board` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are disinterested directors with respect to the act or transaction?
      `a disinterested committee approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a committee of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board determined to be disinterested with respect to the act or transaction, approve or recommend it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the disinterested directors authorize the act or transaction as the Law requires` IS
    `s 144(a)(1) the disinterested directors authorized the act or transaction` `the facts`
    WHERE
        `the facts` MEANS `s 144(a) Facts` WITH
            `the material facts as to the director's or officer's relationship or interest and as to the act or transaction are disclosed or are known to all members of the board of directors or committee` IS `the facts were disclosed or known`
            `the board of directors or committee authorized the act or transaction in good faith` IS `the body acted in good faith`
            `the board of directors or committee authorized the act or transaction without gross negligence` IS `the body was not grossly negligent`
            `the number of disinterested directors then serving on the board of directors or committee that authorized the act or transaction` IS `disinterested directors serving`
            `the number of those disinterested directors who voted in favor` IS `disinterested directors in favor`
            `the number of directors then serving on the board of directors` IS `directors on the board`
            `the number of those directors who are disinterested directors with respect to the act or transaction` IS `disinterested directors on the board`
            `a committee of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the act or transaction, approved or recommended it` IS `a disinterested committee approved`
            -- Placeholders: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `the act or transaction involves or is between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries and 1 or more of the corporation's directors or officers` IS TRUE
            `the act or transaction involves or is between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries and another entity in which 1 or more of its directors or officers are directors, stockholders, partners, managers, members, or officers, or have a financial interest` IS FALSE
            `the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction under subsection (b) or (c)` IS FALSE
            `the votes of the disinterested stockholders` IS `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders` WITH
                `the act or transaction is an offer contemplated by section 251(h)` IS FALSE
                `the vote was informed` IS FALSE
                `the vote was uncoerced` IS FALSE
                `the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders` IS 0
                `the votes cast in favor by the disinterested stockholders` IS 0
                `the number of shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS 0
                `the number of shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders not irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS 0
            `the act or transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders` IS FALSE

-- Protected if it was approved in one of the three ways; open to relief if it was not. Answer nothing for a controlling stockholder transaction or an act outside that description.
@export Is an act or transaction in which the corporation and a director or officer, or an entity of theirs, are on the two sides protected from equitable relief and from damages against a director or officer (s 144(a))?
GIVEN `a director or officer is on the other side` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act or transaction involve or lie between the corporation (or a subsidiary) and 1 or more of its directors or officers?
      `an entity of a director or officer is on the other side` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it involve or lie between the corporation (or a subsidiary) and another entity in which 1 or more directors or officers are directors, stockholders, partners, managers, members or officers, or have a financial interest?
      `it is a controlling stockholder transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a controlling stockholder transaction under subsection (b) or (c)?
      `the facts were disclosed or known` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the material facts as to the director's or officer's relationship or interest and as to the act or transaction disclosed or known to all members of the board or committee?
      `the body acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board or committee authorize the act or transaction in good faith?
      `the body was not grossly negligent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it do so without gross negligence?
      `disinterested directors serving` IS A NUMBER @desc How many disinterested directors were then serving on the board or on the committee that authorized it?
      `disinterested directors in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them voted in favor?
      `directors on the board` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors were then serving on the board?
      `disinterested directors on the board` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them are disinterested directors with respect to the act or transaction?
      `a disinterested committee approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a committee of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board determined to be disinterested, approve or recommend it?
      `it is a section 251(h) offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act or transaction an offer contemplated by section 251(h)?
      `the vote was informed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vote of the disinterested stockholders informed?
      `the vote was uncoerced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it uncoerced?
      `votes cast` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes did the disinterested stockholders cast? (ignored for a section 251(h) offer)
      `votes cast in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those votes were in favor? (ignored for a section 251(h) offer)
      `shares irrevocably accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc For a section 251(h) offer: how many shares have been irrevocably accepted?
      `disinterested shares not accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc For a section 251(h) offer: how many shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders have not been irrevocably accepted?
      `it is fair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act or transaction fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an act or transaction in which a director or officer is interested protected from equitable relief and damages` IS
    `s 144(a) the act or transaction may not be the subject of equitable relief or give rise to damages against a director or officer` `the facts`
    WHERE
        `the facts` MEANS `s 144(a) Facts` WITH
            `the act or transaction involves or is between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries and 1 or more of the corporation's directors or officers` IS `a director or officer is on the other side`
            `the act or transaction involves or is between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries and another entity in which 1 or more of its directors or officers are directors, stockholders, partners, managers, members, or officers, or have a financial interest` IS `an entity of a director or officer is on the other side`
            `the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction under subsection (b) or (c)` IS `it is a controlling stockholder transaction`
            `the material facts as to the director's or officer's relationship or interest and as to the act or transaction are disclosed or are known to all members of the board of directors or committee` IS `the facts were disclosed or known`
            `the board of directors or committee authorized the act or transaction in good faith` IS `the body acted in good faith`
            `the board of directors or committee authorized the act or transaction without gross negligence` IS `the body was not grossly negligent`
            `the number of disinterested directors then serving on the board of directors or committee that authorized the act or transaction` IS `disinterested directors serving`
            `the number of those disinterested directors who voted in favor` IS `disinterested directors in favor`
            `the number of directors then serving on the board of directors` IS `directors on the board`
            `the number of those directors who are disinterested directors with respect to the act or transaction` IS `disinterested directors on the board`
            `a committee of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the act or transaction, approved or recommended it` IS `a disinterested committee approved`
            `the votes of the disinterested stockholders` IS `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders` WITH
                `the act or transaction is an offer contemplated by section 251(h)` IS `it is a section 251(h) offer`
                `the vote was informed` IS `the vote was informed`
                `the vote was uncoerced` IS `the vote was uncoerced`
                `the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders` IS `votes cast`
                `the votes cast in favor by the disinterested stockholders` IS `votes cast in favor`
                `the number of shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS `shares irrevocably accepted`
                `the number of shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders not irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS `disinterested shares not accepted`
            `the act or transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders` IS `it is fair`

-- (b) and (c): controlling stockholder transactions. One record, three questions: the committee limb, the stockholder limb, and the whole.
@export Did a committee of disinterested directors approve the controlling stockholder transaction as the Law requires (s 144(b)(1))?
GIVEN `the facts were disclosed to the committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the material facts as to the transaction, including the controlling stockholder's or control group's interest, disclosed or known to all members of the committee?
      `the board delegated the authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board expressly delegate to the committee the authority to negotiate (or oversee the negotiation of) and to reject the transaction?
      `the committee acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the committee approve or recommend it in good faith?
      `the committee was not grossly negligent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it do so without gross negligence?
      `disinterested directors on the committee` IS A NUMBER @desc How many disinterested directors were then serving on the committee?
      `of them approved` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them approved or recommended the transaction?
      `the committee is two disinterested directors or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the committee consist of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did a committee of disinterested directors approve the controlling stockholder transaction as the Law requires` IS
    `s 144(b)(1) the committee of disinterested directors approved the controlling stockholder transaction` `the transaction`
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS `s 144(b) Facts` WITH
            `the material facts as to the controlling stockholder transaction, including the controlling stockholder's or control group's interest, are disclosed or are known to all members of the committee` IS `the facts were disclosed to the committee`
            `the board of directors expressly delegated to the committee the authority to negotiate (or oversee the negotiation of) and to reject the controlling stockholder transaction` IS `the board delegated the authority`
            `the committee approved or recommended the transaction in good faith` IS `the committee acted in good faith`
            `the committee approved or recommended the transaction without gross negligence` IS `the committee was not grossly negligent`
            `the number of disinterested directors then serving on the committee` IS `disinterested directors on the committee`
            `the number of those disinterested directors who approved or recommended the transaction` IS `of them approved`
            `the committee consists of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the transaction` IS `the committee is two disinterested directors or more`
            -- Placeholders: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction` IS TRUE
            `the act or transaction is a going private transaction` IS FALSE
            `the transaction is conditioned, by its terms as in effect at the time it is submitted to stockholders, on approval or ratification by disinterested stockholders` IS FALSE
            `the votes of the disinterested stockholders` IS `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders` WITH
                `the act or transaction is an offer contemplated by section 251(h)` IS FALSE
                `the vote was informed` IS FALSE
                `the vote was uncoerced` IS FALSE
                `the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders` IS 0
                `the votes cast in favor by the disinterested stockholders` IS 0
                `the number of shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS 0
                `the number of shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders not irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS 0
            `the transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders` IS FALSE

@export Did the disinterested stockholders approve the controlling stockholder transaction, as its terms conditioned, by an informed, uncoerced majority of the votes cast (s 144(b)(2))?
GIVEN `it was conditioned on their approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction conditioned, by its terms as in effect when it was submitted to stockholders, on approval or ratification by disinterested stockholders?
      `it is a section 251(h) offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction an offer contemplated by section 251(h)?
      `the vote was informed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vote informed?
      `the vote was uncoerced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vote uncoerced?
      `votes cast` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes did the disinterested stockholders cast? (ignored for a section 251(h) offer)
      `votes cast in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those votes were in favor? (ignored for a section 251(h) offer)
      `shares irrevocably accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc For a section 251(h) offer: how many shares have been irrevocably accepted?
      `disinterested shares not accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc For a section 251(h) offer: how many shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders have not been irrevocably accepted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the disinterested stockholders approve the controlling stockholder transaction, as its terms conditioned, by an informed, uncoerced majority of the votes cast` IS
    `s 144(b)(2) the disinterested stockholders approved the controlling stockholder transaction as it conditioned` `the transaction`
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS `s 144(b) Facts` WITH
            `the transaction is conditioned, by its terms as in effect at the time it is submitted to stockholders, on approval or ratification by disinterested stockholders` IS `it was conditioned on their approval`
            `the votes of the disinterested stockholders` IS `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders` WITH
                `the act or transaction is an offer contemplated by section 251(h)` IS `it is a section 251(h) offer`
                `the vote was informed` IS `the vote was informed`
                `the vote was uncoerced` IS `the vote was uncoerced`
                `the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders` IS `votes cast`
                `the votes cast in favor by the disinterested stockholders` IS `votes cast in favor`
                `the number of shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS `shares irrevocably accepted`
                `the number of shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders not irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS `disinterested shares not accepted`
            -- Placeholders: the rule called does not read these fields.
            `the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction` IS TRUE
            `the act or transaction is a going private transaction` IS FALSE
            `the material facts as to the controlling stockholder transaction, including the controlling stockholder's or control group's interest, are disclosed or are known to all members of the committee` IS FALSE
            `the board of directors expressly delegated to the committee the authority to negotiate (or oversee the negotiation of) and to reject the controlling stockholder transaction` IS FALSE
            `the committee approved or recommended the transaction in good faith` IS FALSE
            `the committee approved or recommended the transaction without gross negligence` IS FALSE
            `the number of disinterested directors then serving on the committee` IS 0
            `the number of those disinterested directors who approved or recommended the transaction` IS 0
            `the committee consists of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the transaction` IS FALSE
            `the transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders` IS FALSE

-- Protected if the committee approved it, the disinterested stockholders approved it as it conditioned, or it is fair. Answer nothing for a going private transaction or a transaction that is not a controlling stockholder transaction.
@export Is a controlling stockholder transaction that is not a going private transaction protected from equitable relief and from damages on a fiduciary claim against a director, officer, controlling stockholder or member of a control group (s 144(b))?
GIVEN `it is a controlling stockholder transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a controlling stockholder transaction (section 144(e)(3))?
      `it is a going private transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a going private transaction (section 144(e)(6))?
      `the facts were disclosed to the committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the material facts as to the transaction, including the controlling stockholder's or control group's interest, disclosed or known to all members of the committee?
      `the board delegated the authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board expressly delegate to the committee the authority to negotiate (or oversee the negotiation of) and to reject the transaction?
      `the committee acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the committee approve or recommend it in good faith?
      `the committee was not grossly negligent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it do so without gross negligence?
      `disinterested directors on the committee` IS A NUMBER @desc How many disinterested directors were then serving on the committee?
      `of them approved` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them approved or recommended the transaction?
      `the committee is two disinterested directors or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the committee consist of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the transaction?
      `it was conditioned on their approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction conditioned, by its terms as in effect when it was submitted to stockholders, on approval or ratification by disinterested stockholders?
      `it is a section 251(h) offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction an offer contemplated by section 251(h)?
      `the vote was informed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vote of the disinterested stockholders informed?
      `the vote was uncoerced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it uncoerced?
      `votes cast` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes did the disinterested stockholders cast? (ignored for a section 251(h) offer)
      `votes cast in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those votes were in favor? (ignored for a section 251(h) offer)
      `shares irrevocably accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc For a section 251(h) offer: how many shares have been irrevocably accepted?
      `disinterested shares not accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc For a section 251(h) offer: how many shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders have not been irrevocably accepted?
      `it is fair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a controlling stockholder transaction that is not a going private transaction protected from equitable relief and damages on a fiduciary claim` IS
    `s 144(b) the controlling stockholder transaction may not be the subject of equitable relief or give rise to damages on a fiduciary claim` `the transaction`
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS `s 144(b) Facts` WITH
            `the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction` IS `it is a controlling stockholder transaction`
            `the act or transaction is a going private transaction` IS `it is a going private transaction`
            `the material facts as to the controlling stockholder transaction, including the controlling stockholder's or control group's interest, are disclosed or are known to all members of the committee` IS `the facts were disclosed to the committee`
            `the board of directors expressly delegated to the committee the authority to negotiate (or oversee the negotiation of) and to reject the controlling stockholder transaction` IS `the board delegated the authority`
            `the committee approved or recommended the transaction in good faith` IS `the committee acted in good faith`
            `the committee approved or recommended the transaction without gross negligence` IS `the committee was not grossly negligent`
            `the number of disinterested directors then serving on the committee` IS `disinterested directors on the committee`
            `the number of those disinterested directors who approved or recommended the transaction` IS `of them approved`
            `the committee consists of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the transaction` IS `the committee is two disinterested directors or more`
            `the transaction is conditioned, by its terms as in effect at the time it is submitted to stockholders, on approval or ratification by disinterested stockholders` IS `it was conditioned on their approval`
            `the votes of the disinterested stockholders` IS `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders` WITH
                `the act or transaction is an offer contemplated by section 251(h)` IS `it is a section 251(h) offer`
                `the vote was informed` IS `the vote was informed`
                `the vote was uncoerced` IS `the vote was uncoerced`
                `the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders` IS `votes cast`
                `the votes cast in favor by the disinterested stockholders` IS `votes cast in favor`
                `the number of shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS `shares irrevocably accepted`
                `the number of shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders not irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS `disinterested shares not accepted`
            `the transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders` IS `it is fair`

-- Protected if the committee approved it AND the disinterested stockholders approved it as it conditioned, or it is fair. Answer nothing for a transaction that is not a going private transaction.
@export Is a going private transaction protected from equitable relief and from damages on a fiduciary claim against a director, officer, controlling stockholder or member of a control group (s 144(c))?
GIVEN `it is a controlling stockholder transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a controlling stockholder transaction (section 144(e)(3))?
      `it is a going private transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a going private transaction (section 144(e)(6))?
      `the facts were disclosed to the committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the material facts as to the transaction, including the controlling stockholder's or control group's interest, disclosed or known to all members of the committee?
      `the board delegated the authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the board expressly delegate to the committee the authority to negotiate (or oversee the negotiation of) and to reject the transaction?
      `the committee acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the committee approve or recommend it in good faith?
      `the committee was not grossly negligent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it do so without gross negligence?
      `disinterested directors on the committee` IS A NUMBER @desc How many disinterested directors were then serving on the committee?
      `of them approved` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them approved or recommended the transaction?
      `the committee is two disinterested directors or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the committee consist of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the transaction?
      `it was conditioned on their approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction conditioned, by its terms as in effect when it was submitted to stockholders, on approval or ratification by disinterested stockholders?
      `it is a section 251(h) offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction an offer contemplated by section 251(h)?
      `the vote was informed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vote of the disinterested stockholders informed?
      `the vote was uncoerced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it uncoerced?
      `votes cast` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes did the disinterested stockholders cast? (ignored for a section 251(h) offer)
      `votes cast in favor` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those votes were in favor? (ignored for a section 251(h) offer)
      `shares irrevocably accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc For a section 251(h) offer: how many shares have been irrevocably accepted?
      `disinterested shares not accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc For a section 251(h) offer: how many shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders have not been irrevocably accepted?
      `it is fair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a going private transaction protected from equitable relief and damages on a fiduciary claim` IS
    `s 144(c) the going private transaction may not be the subject of equitable relief or give rise to damages on a fiduciary claim` `the transaction`
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS `s 144(b) Facts` WITH
            `the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction` IS `it is a controlling stockholder transaction`
            `the act or transaction is a going private transaction` IS `it is a going private transaction`
            `the material facts as to the controlling stockholder transaction, including the controlling stockholder's or control group's interest, are disclosed or are known to all members of the committee` IS `the facts were disclosed to the committee`
            `the board of directors expressly delegated to the committee the authority to negotiate (or oversee the negotiation of) and to reject the controlling stockholder transaction` IS `the board delegated the authority`
            `the committee approved or recommended the transaction in good faith` IS `the committee acted in good faith`
            `the committee approved or recommended the transaction without gross negligence` IS `the committee was not grossly negligent`
            `the number of disinterested directors then serving on the committee` IS `disinterested directors on the committee`
            `the number of those disinterested directors who approved or recommended the transaction` IS `of them approved`
            `the committee consists of 2 or more directors, each of whom the board has determined to be a disinterested director with respect to the transaction` IS `the committee is two disinterested directors or more`
            `the transaction is conditioned, by its terms as in effect at the time it is submitted to stockholders, on approval or ratification by disinterested stockholders` IS `it was conditioned on their approval`
            `the votes of the disinterested stockholders` IS `s 144 Votes of the disinterested stockholders` WITH
                `the act or transaction is an offer contemplated by section 251(h)` IS `it is a section 251(h) offer`
                `the vote was informed` IS `the vote was informed`
                `the vote was uncoerced` IS `the vote was uncoerced`
                `the votes cast by the disinterested stockholders` IS `votes cast`
                `the votes cast in favor by the disinterested stockholders` IS `votes cast in favor`
                `the number of shares irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS `shares irrevocably accepted`
                `the number of shares owned or controlled by disinterested stockholders not irrevocably accepted for purchase or exchange pursuant to the offer` IS `disinterested shares not accepted`
            `the transaction is fair as to the corporation and the corporation's stockholders` IS `it is fair`

-- Answer nothing for any other meeting.
@export May interested directors be counted in determining the presence of a quorum at the meeting that authorizes the act or transaction (s 144(d)(1))?
GIVEN `it is a meeting that authorizes the act or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a meeting of the board of directors, or of a committee, which authorizes the act or transaction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May interested directors be counted in determining the presence of a quorum at the meeting that authorizes the act or transaction` IS
    `s 144(d)(1) common or interested directors may be counted in determining the presence of a quorum` `it is a meeting that authorizes the act or transaction`

@export Is this director presumed to be a disinterested director because the corporation's stock is listed (s 144(d)(2))?
GIVEN `our stock is listed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have a class of stock listed on a national securities exchange?
      `the director is a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the director a party to the act or transaction?
      `the board found the director independent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the board determined that the director satisfies the applicable criteria for director independence under the exchange's rules (applied to a controlling stockholder or control group too, where applicable)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this director presumed to be a disinterested director because the corporation's stock is listed` IF
    `s 144(d)(2) the director is presumed to be a disinterested director` `our stock is listed` `the director is a party` `the board found the director independent`

-- Only substantial and particularized facts of a material interest or a material relationship rebut it.
@export Is the presumption that this director is disinterested rebutted (s 144(d)(2))?
GIVEN `particularized facts show a material interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do substantial and particularized facts show that the director has a material interest in the act or transaction?
      `particularized facts show a material relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do substantial and particularized facts show that the director has a material relationship with a person with a material interest in it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the presumption that this director is disinterested rebutted` IF
    `s 144(d)(2) the presumption is rebutted` `particularized facts show a material interest` `particularized facts show a material relationship`

@export Is it evidence that a director is not disinterested that a person with a material interest designated, nominated or voted for the director (s 144(d)(3))?
GIVEN `an interested person designated or voted for the director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person that has a material interest in the act or transaction designate or nominate the director, or vote in the director's election?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it evidence that a director is not disinterested that a person with a material interest designated, nominated or voted for the director` IF
    `s 144(d)(3) the designation, nomination or vote is of itself evidence that the director is not a disinterested director` `an interested person designated or voted for the director`

-- Yes if I own or control a majority of the voting power, or can cause the election of a majority of the board, or own at least a third of the voting power and can exercise managerial authority.
@export May I be deemed a controlling stockholder (s 144(d)(4), (e)(2))?
GIVEN `votes I own or control` IS A NUMBER @desc How much voting power in the election of directors do you own or control, together with your affiliates and associates?
      `all the votes` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the voting power in the election of directors of all the outstanding stock entitled to vote generally in the election of directors?
      `I control a majority of the directors' votes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you own or control a majority in voting power in the election of directors who have a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors?
      `I can cause the election of a majority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right, by contract or otherwise, to cause the election of nominees, selected at your discretion, who constitute a majority of the board (or directors entitled to cast a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors)?
      `I control a third of the directors' votes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you own or control at least 1/3 in voting power in the election of directors who have a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors?
      `I can exercise managerial authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the power to exercise managerial authority over the business and affairs of the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be deemed a controlling stockholder` IS
    `s 144(d)(4) the person may be deemed a controlling stockholder` `my control`
    WHERE
        `my control` MEANS `s 144(e)(2) Facts about a person's control` WITH
            `the voting power in the election of directors that the person owns or controls, together with its affiliates and associates` IS `votes I own or control`
            `the voting power in the election of directors of all the outstanding stock entitled to vote generally in the election of directors` IS `all the votes`
            `the person owns or controls a majority in voting power in the election of directors who have a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors` IS `I control a majority of the directors' votes`
            `the person has the right, by contract or otherwise, to cause the election of nominees selected at its discretion who constitute a majority of the board of directors or directors entitled to cast a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors` IS `I can cause the election of a majority`
            `the person owns or controls at least 1/3 in voting power in the election of directors who have a majority in voting power of the votes of all directors` IS `I control a third of the directors' votes`
            `the person has the power to exercise managerial authority over the business and affairs of the corporation` IS `I can exercise managerial authority`

@export Are we, 2 or more stockholders, a control group (s 144(d)(4), (e)(1))?
GIVEN `the number of us` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons are in the group?
      `none of us is a controlling stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is none of us, alone, a controlling stockholder?
      `we have an understanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are we bound together by an agreement, arrangement, or understanding between or among us?
      `together we are a controlling stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By virtue of it, do we together constitute a controlling stockholder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are we, 2 or more stockholders, a control group` IF
    `s 144(d)(4) the persons may be a control group` `our group`
    WHERE
        `our group` MEANS `s 144(e)(1) Facts about a group of persons` WITH
            `the number of persons in the group` IS `the number of us`
            `none of the persons is a controlling stockholder` IS `none of us is a controlling stockholder`
            `the persons are bound together by an agreement, arrangement, or understanding between or among them` IS `we have an understanding`
            `by virtue of that agreement, arrangement, or understanding the persons constitute a controlling stockholder` IS `together we are a controlling stockholder`

@export Is this act or transaction a controlling stockholder transaction (s 144(e)(3))?
GIVEN `it is between the corporation and a controlling stockholder or group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an act or transaction between the corporation or 1 or more of its subsidiaries, on the 1 hand, and a controlling stockholder or a control group, on the other?
      `a controlling stockholder gets a benefit not shared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an act or transaction from which a controlling stockholder or control group receives a financial or other benefit not shared with the corporation's stockholders generally?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this act or transaction a controlling stockholder transaction` IF
    `s 144(e)(3) the act or transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction` `it is between the corporation and a controlling stockholder or group` `a controlling stockholder gets a benefit not shared`

@export Is this transaction a going private transaction (s 144(e)(6))?
GIVEN `we have registered or listed equity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have a class of equity securities subject to section 12(g) or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, or listed on a national securities exchange?
      `it is a Rule 13e-3 transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a “Rule 13e-3 transaction” as defined in 17 CFR 240.13e-3(a)(3) or any successor provision?
      `it is a controlling stockholder transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a controlling stockholder transaction?
      `it takes out the disinterested stockholders' shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under it, are all or substantially all of the shares held by the disinterested stockholders (but not those of the controlling stockholder or control group) cancelled, converted, purchased, or otherwise acquired, or do they cease to be outstanding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this transaction a going private transaction` IF
    `s 144(e)(6) the transaction is a going private transaction` `the transaction`
    WHERE
        `the transaction` MEANS `s 144(e)(6) Facts about the transaction` WITH
            `the corporation has a class of equity securities subject to section 12(g) or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 or listed on a national securities exchange` IS `we have registered or listed equity`
            `the transaction is a Rule 13e-3 transaction as defined in 17 CFR 240.13e-3(a)(3) or any successor provision` IS `it is a Rule 13e-3 transaction`
            `the transaction is a controlling stockholder transaction` IS `it is a controlling stockholder transaction`
            `all or substantially all of the shares held by the disinterested stockholders, but not those of the controlling stockholder or control group, are cancelled, converted, purchased, or otherwise acquired or cease to be outstanding pursuant to the transaction` IS `it takes out the disinterested stockholders' shares`

@export Am I a disinterested director with respect to this act or transaction (s 144(e)(4))?
GIVEN `I am a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the act or transaction?
      `I have a material interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a material interest in the act or transaction?
      `I have a material relationship with an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a material relationship with a person that has a material interest in it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a disinterested director with respect to this act or transaction` IF
    `s 144(e)(4) the director is a disinterested director` `I am a party` `I have a material interest` `I have a material relationship with an interested person`

@export Am I a disinterested stockholder with respect to this act or transaction (s 144(e)(5))?
GIVEN `I have a material interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a material interest in the act or transaction at issue?
      `a controlling stockholder or an interested person is involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the act or transaction involve a controlling stockholder or control group, or another person with a material interest (so that a material relationship matters)?
      `I have a material relationship with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a material relationship with the controlling stockholder or other member of the control group, or any other person that has a material interest in it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a disinterested stockholder with respect to this act or transaction` IF
    `s 144(e)(5) the stockholder is a disinterested stockholder` `I have a material interest` `a controlling stockholder or an interested person is involved` `I have a material relationship with them`

@export Does this benefit give me a material interest in the act or transaction (s 144(e)(7))?
GIVEN `I am` IS A `s 144(e) Kind of person for a material interest or relationship` @desc What are you? One of: a director; a stockholder; a person other than a director or stockholder (the choices are named “for the purposes of s 144(e)(7) and (8)”)
      `there is a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an actual or potential benefit to you, including the avoidance of a detriment?
      `it would devolve on everyone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it one which would devolve on the corporation or the stockholders generally?
      `it would impair my objectivity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a director: would it reasonably be expected to impair the objectivity of your judgment when participating in the negotiation, authorization or approval of the act or transaction?
      `it is material to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a stockholder or other person: would it be material to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this benefit give me a material interest in the act or transaction` IF
    `s 144(e)(7) the person has a material interest` `I am` `there is a benefit` `it would devolve on everyone` `it would impair my objectivity` `it is material to me`

-- Answer nothing if I am neither a director nor a stockholder.
@export Does this relationship give me a material relationship with the person (s 144(e)(8))?
GIVEN `I am` IS A `s 144(e) Kind of person for a material interest or relationship` @desc What are you? One of: a director; a stockholder; a person other than a director or stockholder (the choices are named “for the purposes of s 144(e)(7) and (8)”)
      `it would impair my objectivity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a director: would the familial, financial, professional, employment or other relationship reasonably be expected to impair the objectivity of your judgment when participating in the negotiation, authorization or approval of the act or transaction?
      `it is material to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a stockholder: would the relationship be material to you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this relationship give me a material relationship with the person` IS
    `s 144(e)(8) the person has a material relationship` `I am` `it would impair my objectivity` `it is material to me`

-- Answer nothing if I am neither.
@export Am I shielded from monetary damages as a controlling stockholder or member of a control group for this kind of breach of fiduciary duty (s 144(d)(5))?
GIVEN `I am a controlling stockholder or control group member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a controlling stockholder or a member of a control group?
      `the kind of breach` IS A `s 144(d)(5) Kind of breach` @desc What kind of breach is alleged? One of: a breach of the duty of loyalty to the corporation or the other stockholders; acts or omissions not in good faith or which involve intentional misconduct or a knowing violation of law; a transaction from which you derived an improper personal benefit; a breach of fiduciary duty of any other kind
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I shielded from monetary damages as a controlling stockholder or member of a control group for this kind of breach of fiduciary duty` IS
    `s 144(d)(5) the person is shielded from monetary damages for the breach` `I am a controlling stockholder or control group member` `the kind of breach`

-- Answer nothing for a ground of any other kind.
@export Can I still seek relief on this ground even if the act or transaction was approved under section 144(a), (b) or (c) (s 144(d)(6))?
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `s 144(d)(6) Ground of a claim` @desc What is the ground? One of: that it was not authorized or approved in compliance with the procedures set forth in the chapter; with the certificate of incorporation or bylaws; that it violates a plan, agreement or order of a governmental authority to which the corporation is a party or subject; that a provision or device designed to deter, delay or preclude a change of control is challenged for injunctive relief; that a stockholder or other person knowingly aided and abetted a breach of fiduciary duty by 1 or more directors; a ground of any other kind
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still seek relief on this ground even if the act or transaction was approved under section 144(a), (b) or (c)` IS
    `s 144(d)(6) subsections (a), (b) and (c) leave the right to seek relief on the ground open` `the ground`

§§ `Indemnification and insurance (s 145)`

-- Answer nothing for an amount of any other kind than expenses, judgments, fines and amounts paid in settlement.
@export May my corporation indemnify me against this amount in a proceeding that is not by or in the right of the corporation (s 145(a))?
GIVEN `I am a party or threatened to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was or am I a party, or threatened to be made a party, to a threatened, pending or completed action, suit or proceeding, whether civil, criminal, administrative or investigative?
      `it is by or in the right of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action, suit or proceeding one by or in the right of the corporation?
      `it is because of my role` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by reason of the fact that I am or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or am or was serving at its request as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise?
      `the kind of amount` IS A `s 145 Kind of amount` @desc What is the amount? One of: expenses (including attorneys' fees); judgments; fines; amounts paid in settlement; an amount of any other kind
      `it was actually and reasonably incurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the amount actually and reasonably incurred by me in connection with the action, suit or proceeding?
      `I acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I act in good faith?
      `I reasonably believed it was in the corporation's interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I act in a manner I reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation?
      `it is criminal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action or proceeding criminal?
      `I had no reasonable cause to believe it unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is criminal: did I have no reasonable cause to believe my conduct was unlawful?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation indemnify me against this amount in a proceeding that is not by or in the right of the corporation` IS
    `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` `my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 145(a) Facts` WITH
            `the person was or is a party, or is threatened to be made a party, to a threatened, pending or completed action, suit or proceeding, whether civil, criminal, administrative or investigative` IS `I am a party or threatened to be`
            `the action, suit or proceeding is one by or in the right of the corporation` IS `it is by or in the right of the corporation`
            `the person is a party or threatened by reason of the fact that the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise` IS `it is because of my role`
            `the kind of amount` IS `the kind of amount`
            `the amount was actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the action, suit or proceeding` IS `it was actually and reasonably incurred`
            `the person acted in good faith` IS `I acted in good faith`
            `the person acted in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation` IS `I reasonably believed it was in the corporation's interest`
            `the action or proceeding is criminal` IS `it is criminal`
            `the person had no reasonable cause to believe the person's conduct was unlawful` IS `I had no reasonable cause to believe it unlawful`

-- Answer nothing if it ended in any other way than those named.
@export Does the way the proceeding ended, of itself, create a presumption that I did not act in good faith (s 145(a))?
GIVEN `the way the proceeding ended` IS A `s 145(a) Way a proceeding ended` @desc How did it end? One of: by judgment; by order; by settlement; by conviction; upon a plea of nolo contendere or its equivalent; in any other way
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the way the proceeding ended, of itself, create a presumption that I did not act in good faith` IS
    `s 145(a) the way the proceeding ended of itself creates a presumption that the person did not act in good faith` `the way the proceeding ended`

@export May my corporation indemnify me against my expenses in an action or suit by or in the right of the corporation (s 145(b))?
GIVEN `I am a party or threatened to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was or am I a party, or threatened to be made a party, to a threatened, pending or completed action or suit by or in the right of the corporation to procure a judgment in its favor?
      `it is because of my role` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by reason of the fact that I am or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or am or was serving at its request as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise?
      `my expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the expenses (including attorneys' fees) I actually and reasonably incurred in connection with the defense or settlement of the action or suit?
      `I acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I act in good faith?
      `I reasonably believed it was in the corporation's interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I act in a manner I reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation?
      `I have been adjudged liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have I been adjudged to be liable to the corporation in respect of the claim, issue or matter?
      `the court found me fairly entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: has the Court of Chancery (or the court in which the action or suit was brought) determined upon application that, despite the adjudication but in view of all the circumstances, I am fairly and reasonably entitled to indemnity for expenses?
      `the expenses the court deemed proper` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what are the expenses the court deemed proper?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation indemnify me against my expenses in an action or suit by or in the right of the corporation` IF
    `s 145(b) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against expenses` `my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 145(b) Facts` WITH
            `the person was or is a party, or is threatened to be made a party, to a threatened, pending or completed action or suit by or in the right of the corporation to procure a judgment in its favor` IS `I am a party or threatened to be`
            `the person is a party or threatened by reason of the fact that the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise` IS `it is because of my role`
            `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense or settlement of the action or suit` IS `my expenses`
            `the person acted in good faith` IS `I acted in good faith`
            `the person acted in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation` IS `I reasonably believed it was in the corporation's interest`
            `the person has been adjudged to be liable to the corporation in respect of the claim, issue or matter` IS `I have been adjudged liable`
            `the Court of Chancery or the court in which the action or suit was brought has determined upon application that, despite the adjudication of liability but in view of all the circumstances, the person is fairly and reasonably entitled to indemnity for expenses` IS `the court found me fairly entitled`
            `the expenses the court has deemed proper` IS `the expenses the court deemed proper`

@export What is the most my corporation may indemnify me against in an action or suit by or in the right of the corporation (s 145(b))?
GIVEN `I am a party or threatened to be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was or am I a party, or threatened to be made a party, to a threatened, pending or completed action or suit by or in the right of the corporation to procure a judgment in its favor?
      `it is because of my role` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it by reason of the fact that I am or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or am or was serving at its request as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise?
      `my expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the expenses (including attorneys' fees) I actually and reasonably incurred in connection with the defense or settlement of the action or suit?
      `I acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I act in good faith?
      `I reasonably believed it was in the corporation's interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I act in a manner I reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation?
      `I have been adjudged liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have I been adjudged to be liable to the corporation in respect of the claim, issue or matter?
      `the court found me fairly entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: has the Court of Chancery (or the court in which the action or suit was brought) determined upon application that, despite the adjudication but in view of all the circumstances, I am fairly and reasonably entitled to indemnity for expenses?
      `the expenses the court deemed proper` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: what are the expenses the court deemed proper?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my corporation may indemnify me against in an action or suit by or in the right of the corporation` IS
    `s 145(b) the most the corporation has power to indemnify against expenses` `my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 145(b) Facts` WITH
            `the person was or is a party, or is threatened to be made a party, to a threatened, pending or completed action or suit by or in the right of the corporation to procure a judgment in its favor` IS `I am a party or threatened to be`
            `the person is a party or threatened by reason of the fact that the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise` IS `it is because of my role`
            `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense or settlement of the action or suit` IS `my expenses`
            `the person acted in good faith` IS `I acted in good faith`
            `the person acted in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation` IS `I reasonably believed it was in the corporation's interest`
            `the person has been adjudged to be liable to the corporation in respect of the claim, issue or matter` IS `I have been adjudged liable`
            `the Court of Chancery or the court in which the action or suit was brought has determined upon application that, despite the adjudication of liability but in view of all the circumstances, the person is fairly and reasonably entitled to indemnity for expenses` IS `the court found me fairly entitled`
            `the expenses the court has deemed proper` IS `the expenses the court deemed proper`

@export Must my corporation indemnify me against the expenses of my defense because I was successful (s 145(c)(1))?
GIVEN `I am a present or former director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am I a present or former director of the corporation?
      `I am a present or former officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am I a present or former officer of the corporation?
      `the date of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the act or omission?
      `I am deemed to have consented to service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act or omission, am I deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to 10 Del. C. section 3114(b)?
      `I was successful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have I been successful on the merits or otherwise in defense of the action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b), or of a claim, issue or matter in it?
      `my expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the expenses (including attorneys' fees) I actually and reasonably incurred in connection with the defense?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation indemnify me against the expenses of my defense because I was successful` IF
    `s 145(c)(1) the person must be indemnified against the expenses` `my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 145(c) Facts` WITH
            `the person is a present or former director of the corporation` IS `I am a present or former director`
            `the person is a present or former officer of the corporation` IS `I am a present or former officer`
            `the date of the act or omission` IS `the date of the act or omission`
            `at the time of the act or omission the person is deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to 10 Del. C. section 3114(b)` IS `I am deemed to have consented to service`
            `the person has been successful on the merits or otherwise in defense of the action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b), or of a claim, issue or matter therein` IS `I was successful`
            `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense` IS `my expenses`

@export How much must my corporation indemnify me for the expenses of my defense because I was successful (s 145(c)(1))?
GIVEN `I am a present or former director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am I a present or former director of the corporation?
      `I am a present or former officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am I a present or former officer of the corporation?
      `the date of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the act or omission?
      `I am deemed to have consented to service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act or omission, am I deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to 10 Del. C. section 3114(b)?
      `I was successful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have I been successful on the merits or otherwise in defense of the action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b), or of a claim, issue or matter in it?
      `my expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the expenses (including attorneys' fees) I actually and reasonably incurred in connection with the defense?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must my corporation indemnify me for the expenses of my defense because I was successful` IS
    `s 145(c)(1) the expenses the person must be indemnified against` `my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 145(c) Facts` WITH
            `the person is a present or former director of the corporation` IS `I am a present or former director`
            `the person is a present or former officer of the corporation` IS `I am a present or former officer`
            `the date of the act or omission` IS `the date of the act or omission`
            `at the time of the act or omission the person is deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to 10 Del. C. section 3114(b)` IS `I am deemed to have consented to service`
            `the person has been successful on the merits or otherwise in defense of the action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b), or of a claim, issue or matter therein` IS `I was successful`
            `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense` IS `my expenses`

@export May my corporation indemnify me against the expenses of my defense because I was successful, though I am not a director or an officer within section 145(c)(1) (s 145(c)(2))?
GIVEN `I am a present or former director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am I a present or former director of the corporation?
      `I am a present or former officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am I a present or former officer of the corporation?
      `the date of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the act or omission?
      `I am deemed to have consented to service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act or omission, am I deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to 10 Del. C. section 3114(b)?
      `I was successful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have I been successful on the merits or otherwise in defense of the action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b), or of a claim, issue or matter in it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation indemnify me against the expenses of my defense because I was successful, though I am not a director or an officer within section 145(c)(1)` IF
    `s 145(c)(2) the corporation may indemnify the person against the expenses` `my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 145(c) Facts` WITH
            `the person is a present or former director of the corporation` IS `I am a present or former director`
            `the person is a present or former officer of the corporation` IS `I am a present or former officer`
            `the date of the act or omission` IS `the date of the act or omission`
            `at the time of the act or omission the person is deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to 10 Del. C. section 3114(b)` IS `I am deemed to have consented to service`
            `the person has been successful on the merits or otherwise in defense of the action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b), or of a claim, issue or matter therein` IS `I was successful`
            -- Placeholder: the rule called does not read this field.
            `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense` IS 0

-- A court order is always enough; otherwise a determination in the specific case by the persons the Law names is needed if I am a director or officer when it is made.
@export May my corporation make the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) in my case (s 145(d))?
GIVEN `a court ordered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the indemnification ordered by a court?
      `I am a director or officer now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am I a director or officer of the corporation at the time of the determination?
      `the determination was made in my specific case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the determination made as authorized in the specific case?
      `it found I met the standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the determination that I met the applicable standard of conduct set forth in subsections (a) and (b)?
      `who decided` IS A `s 145(d) Who made the determination` @desc Who made the determination? One of: a majority vote of the directors who are not parties to the action, suit or proceeding, even though less than a quorum; a committee of such directors designated by majority vote of such directors, even though less than a quorum; independent legal counsel in a written opinion; the stockholders; someone else
      `the committee was designated by the non-party directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a committee: was it designated by majority vote of the directors who are not parties?
      `there are no directors who are not parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there no directors who are not parties to the action, suit or proceeding?
      `the non-party directors directed counsel to decide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors who are not parties direct that independent legal counsel make the determination?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation make the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) in my case` IF
    `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` `my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 145(d) Facts` WITH
            `the indemnification is ordered by a court` IS `a court ordered it`
            `the person is a director or officer of the corporation at the time of the determination` IS `I am a director or officer now`
            `the determination was made as authorized in the specific case` IS `the determination was made in my specific case`
            `the determination is that the person has met the applicable standard of conduct set forth in subsections (a) and (b)` IS `it found I met the standard`
            `who made the determination` IS `who decided`
            `the committee was designated by majority vote of the directors who are not parties` IS `the committee was designated by the non-party directors`
            `there are no directors who are not parties to the action, suit or proceeding` IS `there are no directors who are not parties`
            `the directors who are not parties directed that independent legal counsel make the determination` IS `the non-party directors directed counsel to decide`

-- Answer nothing if the expenses were not for defending an action, suit or proceeding, or if I am in neither class the Law names.
@export May my corporation pay my expenses of defending the proceeding before its final disposition (s 145(e))?
GIVEN `I am a present director or officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am I a present officer or director of the corporation?
      `I am a former director or officer or another agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am I a former director or officer, or another employee or agent of the corporation, or a person serving at its request as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise?
      `they are for defending a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the expenses (including attorneys' fees) incurred in defending a civil, criminal, administrative or investigative action, suit or proceeding?
      `the corporation has my undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation received an undertaking by or on behalf of me, as a director or officer, to repay the amount if it is ultimately determined that I am not entitled to be indemnified by the corporation as authorized in this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation pay my expenses of defending the proceeding before its final disposition` IS
    `s 145(e) the corporation may pay the expenses in advance of the final disposition` `my case`
    WHERE
        `my case` MEANS `s 145(e) Facts` WITH
            `the person is a present officer or director of the corporation` IS `I am a present director or officer`
            `the person is a former director or officer, or another employee or agent of the corporation, or a person serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise` IS `I am a former director or officer or another agent`
            `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) were incurred in defending a civil, criminal, administrative or investigative action, suit or proceeding` IS `they are for defending a proceeding`
            `the corporation has received an undertaking by or on behalf of the director or officer to repay the amount if it shall ultimately be determined that the person is not entitled to be indemnified by the corporation as authorized in this section` IS `the corporation has my undertaking`

@export Are my rights to indemnification and advancement under section 145 the only ones I have (s 145(f))?
GIVEN `I have another right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do I have another right to indemnification or advancement of expenses under a bylaw, agreement, vote of stockholders or disinterested directors or otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my rights to indemnification and advancement under section 145 the only ones I have` IF
    `s 145(f) the other subsections of this section are the exclusive source of the person's rights` `I have another right`

@export Is my right to indemnification or advancement protected from later elimination or impairment (s 145(f))?
GIVEN `where the right is given` IS A `Where a provision is made` @desc Where is the provision giving the right made? One of: in the certificate of incorporation; in the bylaws; in a resolution of the board of directors; in none of these
      `the date of the act or omission` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the act or omission?
      `the date of the amendment` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the provision amended, repealed or eliminated?
      `it authorized impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the provision in effect at the time of the act or omission explicitly authorize elimination or impairment after the act or omission had occurred?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my right to indemnification or advancement protected from later elimination or impairment` IF
    `s 145(f) the right is protected from elimination or impairment by the later amendment, repeal or elimination` `where the right is given` `the date of the act or omission` `the date of the amendment` `it authorized impairment`

-- Answer nothing if I am not a director, officer, employee or agent.
@export May my corporation buy insurance on my behalf for liability asserted against me because of my role (s 145(g))?
GIVEN `I am or was in a role` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am or was I a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or serving at its request as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise?
      `the corporation could indemnify me against it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the corporation have power to indemnify me against the liability under this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation buy insurance on my behalf for liability asserted against me because of my role` IS
    `s 145(g) the corporation has power to purchase and maintain insurance on behalf of the person` `I am or was in a role` `the corporation could indemnify me against it`

@export Does insurance through a captive insurance company count as insurance for the power to insure (s 145(g))?
GIVEN `it is through a captive insurer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the insurance provided directly or indirectly by or through a captive insurance company?
      `the captive is licensed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the captive insurance company organized and licensed in compliance with the laws of a jurisdiction?
      `it excludes fraud and improper profit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms exclude coverage for, and provide that the insurer shall not pay, loss arising out of a personal profit or financial advantage to which the person was not legally entitled, or a deliberate criminal or deliberate fraudulent act or a knowing violation of law, if established by a final, nonappealable adjudication in the underlying proceeding (not an action to determine coverage), unless and only to the extent the person is entitled to be indemnified under this section?
      `it requires an independent decision on current directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms require that a determination to make a payment in respect of a claim against a current director or officer be made by an independent claims administrator or in accordance with paragraphs (d)(1) through (4)?
      `it requires notice to stockholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the terms require that, before a payment in connection with a dismissal or compromise of an action, suit or proceeding by or in the right of the corporation as to which notice is required to be given to stockholders, the corporation include in the notice that a payment is proposed to be made under the insurance?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does insurance through a captive insurance company count as insurance for section 145(g)` IF
    `s 145(g) the insurance is insurance for the purposes of this subsection` `the insurance`
    WHERE
        `the insurance` MEANS `s 145(g) Facts about insurance through a captive insurance company` WITH
            `the insurance is provided directly or indirectly by or through a captive insurance company` IS `it is through a captive insurer`
            `the captive insurance company is organized and licensed in compliance with the laws of a jurisdiction` IS `the captive is licensed`
            `the terms exclude coverage for, and provide that the insurer shall not pay, loss arising out of a personal profit or financial advantage to which the person was not legally entitled, or a deliberate criminal or deliberate fraudulent act or a knowing violation of law, if established by a final, nonappealable adjudication in the underlying proceeding (not an action or proceeding to determine coverage), unless and only to the extent the person is entitled to be indemnified under this section` IS `it excludes fraud and improper profit`
            `the terms require that a determination to make a payment in respect of a claim against a current director or officer be made by an independent claims administrator or in accordance with paragraphs (d)(1) through (4)` IS `it requires an independent decision on current directors`
            `the terms require that, before a payment in connection with a dismissal or compromise of an action, suit or proceeding by or in the right of the corporation as to which notice is required to be given to stockholders, the corporation include in the notice that a payment is proposed to be made under the insurance` IS `it requires notice to stockholders`

@export Is another insured person's conduct imputed to me for the conditions on captive insurance (s 145(g))?
GIVEN `the conduct is another insured person's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the conduct the conduct of another insured person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is another insured person's conduct imputed to me for the captive-insurance conditions of section 145(g)(1)` IF
    `s 145(g) the conduct of an insured person is imputed to another insured person for the purposes of paragraph (g)(1)` `the conduct is another insured person's`

@export Does my corporation become subject to Title 18 solely because it maintains a captive insurance company that insures under section 145 (s 145(g))?
GIVEN `it maintains a captive insurer for this` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation establish or maintain a captive insurance company that provides insurance pursuant to this section?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation become subject to Title 18 solely because it maintains a captive insurance company that insures under section 145` IF
    `s 145(g) the corporation is, solely by virtue of the captive insurance company, subject to the provisions of Title 18` `it maintains a captive insurer for this`

-- Answer nothing if the conditions are not met.
@export Do I stand in the same position with respect to the surviving corporation as I did with the constituent corporation (s 145(h))?
GIVEN `my corporation was a constituent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the corporation I served a constituent corporation, or a constituent of a constituent, absorbed in a consolidation or merger?
      `it could have indemnified its people` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would that constituent corporation, if its separate existence had continued, have had power and authority to indemnify its directors, officers, and employees or agents?
      `I served it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Am or was I a director, officer, employee or agent of that constituent corporation, or serving at its request as such of another enterprise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I stand in the same position with respect to the surviving corporation as I did with the constituent corporation` IS
    `s 145(h) the person stands in the same position with respect to the resulting or surviving corporation` `my corporation was a constituent` `it could have indemnified its people` `I served it`

-- Answer nothing for any other matter.
@export Does a reference to an employee benefit plan, an excise tax or service for a plan fall within the references in section 145 (s 145(i))?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 145(i) Employee benefit plan matter` @desc What is the matter? One of: an employee benefit plan, as an other enterprise; an excise tax assessed on a person with respect to an employee benefit plan, as a fine; service as a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation which imposes duties on, or involves services by, the person with respect to an employee benefit plan, its participants or beneficiaries, as serving at the request of the corporation; anything else
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a reference to an employee benefit plan, an excise tax or service for a plan fall within the references in section 145` IS
    `s 145(i) the matter is within the reference` `the matter`

-- Answer nothing if I did not act in good faith and in that belief.
@export Am I deemed to have acted in a manner not opposed to the best interests of the corporation because I acted for an employee benefit plan's participants (s 145(i))?
GIVEN `I acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I act in good faith?
      `I reasonably believed it was for the plan participants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did I act in a manner I reasonably believed to be in the interest of the participants and beneficiaries of an employee benefit plan?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed to have acted in a manner not opposed to the best interests of the corporation because I acted for an employee benefit plan's participants` IS
    `s 145(i) the person is deemed to have acted in a manner not opposed to the best interests of the corporation` `I acted in good faith` `I reasonably believed it was for the plan participants`

@export Does my indemnification and advancement continue after I cease to be a director, officer, employee or agent (s 145(j))?
GIVEN `it was otherwise provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it otherwise provided when the indemnification or advancement was authorized or ratified?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my indemnification and advancement continue after I cease to be a director, officer, employee or agent` IF
    `s 145(j) the indemnification and advancement continue as to a person who has ceased to be a director, officer, employee or agent` `it was otherwise provided`

@export Do my indemnification and advancement pass to my heirs, executors and administrators (s 145(j))?
GIVEN `it was otherwise provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it otherwise provided when the indemnification or advancement was authorized or ratified?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my indemnification and advancement pass to my heirs, executors and administrators` IF
    `s 145(j) the indemnification and advancement inure to the benefit of the heirs, executors and administrators of the person` `it was otherwise provided`

-- Answer nothing if it is not such an action.
@export Does the Court of Chancery have exclusive jurisdiction over my action for advancement or indemnification (s 145(k))?
GIVEN `it is such an action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action for advancement of expenses or for indemnification brought under this section or under a bylaw, agreement, vote of stockholders or disinterested directors, or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Court of Chancery have exclusive jurisdiction over my action for advancement or indemnification` IS
    `s 145(k) the Court of Chancery has exclusive jurisdiction over the action` `it is such an action`

-- Answer nothing if the question is not that obligation.
@export Can the Court of Chancery summarily determine the corporation's obligation to advance my expenses (s 145(k))?
GIVEN `it is the obligation to advance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question the corporation's obligation to advance expenses?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Court of Chancery summarily determine the corporation's obligation to advance my expenses` IS
    `s 145(k) the Court of Chancery may summarily determine the question` `it is the obligation to advance`

§§ `Putting a matter to the stockholders, and approving or ratifying instruments (ss 146 and 147)`

@export May my corporation agree to submit a matter to a vote of its stockholders even though the board no longer recommends it (s 146)?
GIVEN `the board now recommends rejecting it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the board of directors determined, after approving the matter, that it is no longer advisable and recommended that the stockholders reject or vote against it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation agree to submit a matter to a vote of its stockholders even though the board no longer recommends it` IF
    `s 146 the corporation may agree to submit the matter to a vote of its stockholders` `the board now recommends rejecting it`

-- Answer nothing if the Law does not expressly require the board to act, or if the form is some other form.
@export May the board approve an agreement, instrument or document in this form when the Law requires it to approve it (s 147)?
GIVEN `the Law requires the board to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this chapter expressly require the board of directors to approve or take other action with respect to the agreement, instrument or document?
      `the form` IS A `s 147 Form in which the board approves` @desc In what form is it approved? One of: in final form; in substantially final form; in some other form
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board approve an agreement, instrument or document in this form when the Law requires it to approve it` IS
    `s 147 the board of directors may approve the agreement, instrument or document in this form` `the Law requires the board to act` `the form`

@export May the board ratify an agreement, instrument or document it approved, before its filing takes effect (s 147)?
GIVEN `the board has acted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the board of directors acted to approve or take other action with respect to the agreement, instrument or document?
      `it is to be filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it required by this chapter to be filed with the Secretary of State, or referenced in a certificate so filed?
      `the filing is not yet effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the filing with the Secretary of State not yet become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the board ratify an agreement, instrument or document it approved, before its filing takes effect` IF
    `s 147 the board of directors may adopt a resolution ratifying the agreement, instrument or document` `the board has acted` `it is to be filed` `the filing is not yet effective`

@export As of what date is a ratification under section 147 effective (s 147)?
GIVEN `the date of the original approval` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the board of directors originally approve or take other action with respect to the agreement, instrument or document?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `As of what date is a ratification under section 147 effective` IS
    `s 147 the date as of which the ratification is effective` `the date of the original approval`

-- Answer nothing if it is not a ratification under this section.
@export Does a ratification under section 147 satisfy a requirement that the board approve or act in a specific manner or sequence (s 147)?
GIVEN `it is a ratification under section 147` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ratification a ratification under section 147?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a ratification under section 147 satisfy a requirement that the board approve or act in a specific manner or sequence` IS
    `s 147 the ratification satisfies a requirement that the board of directors approve or act in a specific manner or sequence` `it is a ratification under section 147`

@export Is ratification under section 147 the only way to ratify an agreement, instrument or document the board approved under that section (s 147)?
GIVEN `the board approved it under section 147` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement, instrument or document approved by the board of directors pursuant to this section?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is ratification under section 147 the only way to ratify an agreement, instrument or document the board approved under that section` IF
    `s 147 ratification under this section is the exclusive means of ratifying it` `the board approved it under section 147`
